ry differentiation bilaterally.  No calculus or back pressure effect is seen\r\n No intra-abdominal mass lesion is seen. The demonstrated bowel loops, the mesentery and the para-aortic area are within normal limits.\r\nAn anterior abdominal wall defect measuring about 40.5mm is noted in the right inguinal region with mobile bowel loops seen bulging through it. No associated proximal bowel dilatation is noted.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline abut shows normal wall thickness of about 4mm and contained clear urine. \r\nThe prostate is normal in size and shows uniform parenchymal echogenicity and outline. It measures about 37.1ml in volume. \r\nConclusion:  Features suggest right inguinal hernia. \r\n\r\nDR CHIDINMA   08/08/2026\r\nRadiologist','Features suggest right inguinal hernia.','completed','2026-08-08 11:53:33','2026-08-08 11:53:33','2026-08-08 11:53:33'),(246,4159,4170,15,NULL,15,NULL,'2026-08-08 12:12:35','Erratic behavior','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe liver is normal in size measuring about 15.7cm in span with intact capsule. It showed partially coarsened parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal hepatic lesion demonstrated. The biliary tree and hepatic vasculature is normal.  \r\nThe spleen, pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outlines and sizes. They showed normal echogenicity and also show good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes with no back pressure effect or renal masses seen.  No intra abdominal mass lesion seen.\r\nModerate ascitic fluid collection is seen in the peritoneal cavity. \r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline and thickness and contains clear urine.  \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 25.1mm in its widest AP diameter. It shows an intact endometrial plate echo.  No intracavitary collection is seen. \r\nBoth adnexae are within normal limits\r\nConclusion:   Features are suggestive of chronic liver disease with moderate ascitic fluid collection? cause.  Liver function test is advised.                                                                                                    \r\n   \r\nDR CHIDINMA  Radiologist   \r\n08/08/2026','Features are suggestive of chronic liver disease with moderate ascitic fluid collection? cause.  Liver function test is advised.','completed','2026-08-08 12:12:35','2026-08-08 12:12:35','2026-08-08 12:12:35'),(247,4160,4171,15,NULL,15,NULL,'2026-08-08 12:34:30','Left intermittent inguinal swelling in a 7 month old male infant','ABDOMINAL USS \r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, pancreas and spleen. They  are also normal in size and echopattern. No focal mass lesion is noted. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in positions, shapes, sizes and outline. They also showed normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No calculus or back pressure effect is seen\r\n No intra-abdominal mass lesion is seen. The demonstrated bowel loops, the mesentery and the para-aortic area are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline and wall thickness and shows urine containing mobile internal echoes. No calculus is seen within it. \r\nAn anterior abdominal wall defect measuring about 9.69mm is noted in the left inguinal region with bowel loop seen through bulging into it.\r\nBoth testicles were demonstrated and are normal in size .  They show uniform parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. No focal intra-testicular mass lesion or collection seen. The  peritesticular fluid collection is within normal limits bilaterally   \r\nThe visualized scrotal sacs and the epididymes bilaterally are within normal limits.\r\nConclusion:  Features are those of a left inguinal hernia\r\n\r\nDR CHIDINMA   08/08/2026\r\nRadiologist','Features are those of a left inguinal hernia','completed','2026-08-08 12:34:30','2026-08-08 12:34: