paces, extraocular muscles and the optic nerves are within normal limits.','Sonographic features are those of  left retinal detachment  with associated chronic vitreous hemorrhage.','completed','2026-08-17 11:19:18','2026-08-17 11:19:18','2026-08-17 11:19:18'),(602,4529,4540,8,NULL,8,NULL,'2026-08-17 11:22:59','Cyesis','OBSTETRICS USS    \r\nSingle live active intrauterine fetus is demonstrated.\r\nActively changing position.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular.\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is identified.\r\nPlacenta is anterior on the uterine body.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate. \r\nBPD= 41mm, EGA= 18weeks + 3days    EDD= 15/01/2027\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform. \r\nInternal os is closed.','Single viable intra-uterine cyesis at about 18weeks + 3days GA with satisfactory fetal well-being.','completed','2026-08-17 11:22:59','2026-08-17 11:22:59','2026-08-17 11:22:59'),(603,4535,4546,8,NULL,8,NULL,'2026-08-17 11:26:22',NULL,'The liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echopattern. No focal hepatic mass lesion demonstrated. The intrahepatic veins and biliary ducts are within normal limits. Normal portal vein.\r\nThe gallbladder, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits. The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are normal in calibre and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal collection or mass lesion is seen. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size and shows uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. No intra-cavitary collection cyesis or mass lesion identified.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Essentially normal examination','completed','2026-08-17 11:26:22','2026-08-17 11:26:22','2026-08-17 11:26:22'),(604,4532,4543,8,NULL,8,NULL,'2026-08-17 11: