25 18:52:06'),(986,4921,4933,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-08-25 19:15:07','?PID','The demonstrated bowel loops are fluid loaded and showed poor peristalsis presumably due to inflammatory changes. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites seen. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe liver is normal in size and show regular outline with normal parenchymal echotexture and echogenicity. The intra hepatic veins and biliary ducts are not dilated. No focal hepatic lesion demonstrated.\r\nThe spleen, pancreas and para-aortic area are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and sizes. They showed good cortico-medullary differentiation. No calculus seen. The ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and shows regular outline with normal wall thickness. No mass lesion or calculus seen. No mass lesion or calculus seen.\r\nThe uterus, adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of inflammatory bowel changes enteritis.\r\nFurther evaluations are suggested as well.','completed','2026-08-25 19:15:07','2026-08-25 19:15:07','2026-08-25 19:15:07'),(987,4924,4936,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-08-25 20:00:56','Abdominal distension','There is excessive bowel gas especially in upper and central abdomen. However, the demonstrated bowel loops are dilated and show exaggerated peristalsis with to and fro movements of their contents. Mild free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is noted? reactionary. No mass lesion or lymph node is seen.\r\nThe liver is normal in size and echo pattern. The gall bladder contains clear content with regular wall thickness and outline. \r\nThe pancreas and para-aortic region are within normal limits.  \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and shows uniform parenchymal echoes and outline.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They show moderate hydronephrosis with preserved echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus is noted bilaterally.\r\nThe urinary bladder is urine containing multiple mobile echoes with normal wall thickness and regular outline.','Features are those of multi-organs inflammatory changes (cystitis, renal and bowel loops) presumably sepsis with intestinal obstruction. \r\nPlain abdominal x-ray (erect and supine) are advised for further evaluation','completed','2026-08-25 20:00:56','2026-08-25 19:52:21','2026-08-25 20:00:56'),(988,4925,4937,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-08-25 20:13:56','PID','The liver is normal in size and show regular outline with normal parenchymal echotexture and echogenicity. The intra hepatic veins and biliary ducts are not dilated. No focal hepatic lesion demonstrated.\r\nThe spleen, pancreas and para-aortic area are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and sizes. They showed good cortico-medullary differentiation. No calculus seen. The ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are fluid loaded and showed poor peristalsis presumably due to inflammatory changes. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites seen. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and shows regular outline with normal wall thickness. No mass lesion or calculus seen. No mass lesion or calculus seen.\r\nThe uterus, adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of enteritis. \r\nPossibility of PUD cannot be totally rule out.','completed','2026-08-25 20:13:56','2026-08-25 20:13:56','2026-08-25 20:13:56'),(989,4923,4935,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-08-25 20:53:21','Abdominal discomfort','The liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size and empty. It measures about 45mm in its widest AP diamter. The endometrial plate is intact and uniform myometrial echoes. No intracavitory collection or gestational sac noted. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Essentially normal examination. No cyesis currently. Serum PT is advised. \r\nPossibility of right sided pyelonephritis cannot be totally rule out. Further evaluation is suggested.','completed','2026-08-25 20:53:21','2026-08-25 20:52:28','2026-08-25 20:53:21'),(990,4926,4938,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-08-25 21:01:23','CYESIS','Single live intrauterine fetus, in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular,\r\nAdequate liquor volume,\r\nPlacenta is posterior and fundal on the body.\r\nBPD = 96mm, FL = 77mm,\r\nEGA = 39 Weeks + 1 days,\r\nEDD = 31/08/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine fetus at about 39 weeks + 1 day GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-08-25 21:01:23','2026-08-25 21:01:23','2026-08-25 21:01:23'),(991,4928,4940,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-08-26 10:00:56','?Intestinal obstruction','The liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal. The gall bladder is show normal outline and wall thickness.  \r\nThe spleen is normal in size  and show normal echopattern. No focal lesion seen within it.\r\nThe pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and 