estation at about 30 weeks + 3 days GA(Diamniotic monochorionic)','completed','2026-08-31 18:58:55','2026-08-31 18:58:55','2026-08-31 18:58:55'),(1205,5147,5160,13,NULL,13,NULL,'2026-08-31 19:23:16','Pyelonephritis R/O Enteritis','The liver is normal in size and outline. It showed normal parenchymal echotexture and echo reflectivity. The hepatic veins are within normal limits.\r\nThe gall bladder is filled with clear bile. It showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen. The biliary ducts are normal in caliber and luminal echoes.\r\nThe spleen is normal in position, outline and parenchymal echo pattern.\r\nThe pancreas is normal in size and parenchymal echo pattern. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe bowel loops in the lower abdomen are dilated with fluid loading, however it shows preserved peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion is seen. The region of the appendix is within normal limits. There is mild ascites noted.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They showed normal echopattern with good corticomedullary differentiation. No mass lesion or calculus is seen. The collecting system and ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly filled with clear urine and showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe uterus is normal in size and empty measuring about 35 mm in widest AP diameter. It shows uniform myometrial echoes and intact endometrial plate. The adnexae and POD are within normal limit.','Features are suggestive of inflammatory bowel changes presumably due to enterocolitis.','completed','2026-08-31 19:23:16','2026-08-31 19:23:16','2026-08-31 19:23:16'),(1206,5148,5161,13,NULL,13,NULL,'2026-08-31 19:29:44','LAP','The uterus is Bulky containing single intact gestational sac with a single fetus seen within it. \r\nCardiac activity is present. Liquor is adequate for GA\r\nCRL= 48.1 mm  EGA= 12 weeks + 1 day\r\nEDD= 14/03/2027 \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform \r