.','Normal sonographic findings.','completed','2026-09-02 15:20:49','2026-09-02 15:20:49','2026-09-02 15:20:49'),(1289,5236,5249,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 15:54:56','pyelonephritis','The liver enlarged measuring about 189mm in span. It shows irregular outline with coarsened parenchymal echotexture and increased echogenicity. There are multiple intra-hepatic mass lesions demonstrated mainly in the right hepatic lobe, one of which measures about 67x54mm in size(in the segment VI) . The biliary ducts and vascular channels are not dilated. \r\nThe gallbladder, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, position and outline with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus seen.\r\nNo ascites seen. The bowel loops seen are normal in caliber and peristalsis.\r\nThe urinary bladder and prostate are within normal limits.\r\nThe prostate is grossly within normal limit(22.2ml)','Features are suggestive of chronic liver disease with malignant transformation.\r\nFurther evaluation is advised.','completed','2026-09-02 15:54:56','2026-09-02 15:54:56','2026-09-02 15:54:56'),(1290,5237,5250,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 16:05:10','CYESIS','Single live intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear with SDVP =6.6cm (single pocket) \r\nPlacenta is posterior upper uterine body.  \r\nBPD= 87mm, FL= 71mm, AC = 316mm, HC= 317mm all corresponding to an average GA of 35 Weeks + 4 days \r\nEDD= 03/10/2026 \r\nEFW = 2875g\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2','Single live intrauterine fetus at about 35 weeks + 4 days with satisfactory biophysical profile score.','completed','2026-09-02 16:05:10','2026-09-02 16:05:10','2026-09-02 16:05:10'),(1291,5238,5251,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 16:14:31','cyesis','Single live intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently. `\r\ncardiac activity is present and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is posterior on the uterine body. No subchorionic collection seen.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nBPD = 75mm, FL = 59mm\r\nEGA= 30 weeks \r\nEDD = 11/11/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 30 weeks GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-02 16:14:31','2026-09-02 16:14:31','2026-09-02 16:14:31'),(1292,5211,5224,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 16:21:00','No clinical history provided','There is  mild spiking of the intercondylar spines and reduction of the  medial tibiofemoral and patellofemoral joint spaces. Mild marginal articular osteophytes are also noted. \r\nThe fat pads and the bone mineralization are preserved.\r\nNormal overlying soft tissue outline.','Features suggest moderate  left knee osteoarthritis.','completed','2026-09-02 16:21:00','2026-09-02 16:21:00','2026-09-02 16:21:00');
INSERT INTO `bill_results` VALUES (1293,5239,5252,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 16:31:53','UTI r/o appendicitis','The uterus is normal in size measuring about 47mm in its widest AP diameter.  The endometrium is thickened with trilaminar pattern presumably due to menstrual changes. The myometrial echoes are uniform. The internal cervical os is closed. \r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus is noted\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion and ascites is demonstrated. The bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Features are suggestive of endometritis.','completed','2026-09-02 16:31:53','2026-09-02 16:30:14','2026-09-02 16:31:53'),(1294,5240,5253,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 16:34:07','cyesis','Bulky uterus containing single intact gestational sac with a single live fetal pole within it. Cardiac activity noted. \r\nCRL=32.84mm, \r\nEGA=10 weeks+4 days, \r\nEDD=27/03/2027\r\nThe adnexae and POD are within normal limits.\r\nThe internal cervical os is closed.','Single live intrauterine gestation at about 10 weeks+4 days, GA.','completed','2026-09-02 16:34:07','2026-09-02 16:34:07','2026-09-02 16:34:07'),(1295,5241,5254,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 16:52:19','severe epigastric pain? cause','The liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. It measures about 117mm in span. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. Marked probe pressure tenderness is ilicited over the epigastric region.\r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline and are seen floating clear free intraperitoneal fluid collection. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine. No calculus or mass lesion.\r\nThe prostate is grossly normal for age.','Marked probe pressure tenderness over the epigastrium presumably due to Acid peptic disease.\r\nFurther evaluation is advised.','completed','2026-09-02 16:52:19','2026-09-02 16:52:19','2026-09-02 16:52:19'),(1296,5242,5255,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-09-02 17:01:15','abdominal pain? cause','The demonstrated bowel loops in the right abdomen are fluid loaded and showed poor peristalsis presumably due to inflammatory changes. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites seen. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe liver is normal in size and show regular outline with normal parenchymal echotexture and echogenicity. The intra hepatic veins and biliary ducts are not dilated. No focal hepatic lesion demonstrated.\r\nThe spleen, pancreas and para-aortic area are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and sizes. They showed good cortico-medullary differentiation. No calculus seen. The ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and shows regular outline with normal wall thickness. No mass lesion or calculus seen. No mass lesion or calculus seen.','Features are suggestive of entero-colitis.','completed','2026-09-02 17:01:15','2026-09-02 17:01:15','2026-09-02 17:01:15'),(1297,5243,