ndal on the body.\r\nBPD = 81.3mm, FL = 63.8mm,\r\nEGA = 32 Weeks + 5 days,\r\nEDD = 23/10/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine fetus at about 32 weeks + 5 day GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-02 19:27:14','2026-09-02 19:27:14','2026-09-02 19:27:14'),(1300,5246,5259,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-09-02 19:28:41','cyesis dating','Bulky uterus containing a single intact gestational sac with a live fetal pole\r\nCardiac pulsation is present and regular. \r\nCRL = 23.4mm   \r\nEGA= 09 weeks + 3 days \r\nEDD=04/04/2027\r\nInternal os is closed.   \r\nBoth adnexae and POD appear within normal limits.','Early viable intrauterine cyesis at about 09 weeks + 3 days GA.','completed','2026-09-02 19:28:41','2026-09-02 19:28:41','2026-09-02 19:28:41'),(1301,5247,5260,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-09-02 19:31:34','MALARIA R/O UTI','Single live intrauterine fetus, in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular,\r\nNO MEASURABLE AMNIOTIC FLUID POCKET DEMONSTRATED. The uterine wall is seen overlying the fetal body. \r\nPlacenta is anterior on the body.\r\nBPD = 59.4mm, FL = 51mm,\r\nEGA = 25 Weeks + 3 days,\r\nEDD = 13/12/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine fetus at about 25 weeks + 3 day GA WITH SEVERE OLIGOHYDRAMNIOUS.','completed','2026-09-02 19:31:34','2026-09-02 19:31:34','2026-09-02 19:31:34'),(1302,5248,5261,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-09-02 19:42:52','FWB','Single live intrauterine fetus, in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular,\r\nAdequate liquor volume,\r\nPlacenta is posterior on the body.\r\nBPD = 64mm, FL = 64mm,\r\nEGA = 27 Weeks + 1 days,\r\nEDD = 01/12/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine fetus at about 27 weeks + 1 day GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-02 19:42:52','2026-09-02 19:42:52','2026-09-02 19:42:52'),(1303,5249,5262,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-09-02 19:50:37','Acute abdomen? cause','The demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal collection or focal mass lesion seen seen. \r\nMarked epigastric transducer tenderness is elicited,\r\nThe liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus, adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Epigastric transducer tenderness. Consider acute PUD exacerbation as one of your differentials and clinically correlate with other lab findings.','completed','2026-09-02 19:50:37','2026-09-02 19:50:37','2026-09-02 19:50:37'),(1304,5250,5263,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-03 09:32:49','Cyesis','The uterus measures about 42mm in widest AP diameter. It shows homogenous myometrial echotexture. No intracavitary fluid collection is noted.\r\nThe endometrial plate is intact with normal endometrial/myometrial interface. \r\nBoth adnexae are within normal limits. \r\nThe POD is free.','Normal examination ?complete abortion.','completed','2026-09-03 09:32:49','2026-09-03 09:32:49','2026-09-03 09:32:49'),(1305,5252,5265,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-03 09:36:53','?Enteritis','The liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 32mm in its widest AP diameter. It shows intact endometrial plate.  No intracavitary collection focal lesion is seen. \r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Normal sonographic findings.','completed','2026-09-03 09:36:53','2026-09-03 09:36:53','2026-09-03 09:36:53'),(1306,5253,5266,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-03 09:40:55','Fetal well-being','Single live active intrauterine fetus.\r\nActively changing position.`\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is anterior and partly fundal.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nBPD= 33mm,   \r\nEGA = 16 weeks + 1 days, \r\nEDD = 17/01/2027','Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 16 weeks + 1 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-03 09:40:55','2026-09-03 09:40:55','2026-09-03 09:40:55'),(1307,5254,5267,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-03 09:46:37','2 Infertility','The liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 47mm in its widest AP diameter. It shows intact endometrial plate.  No intracavitary collection focal lesion is seen. \r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Normal sonographic findings.','completed','2026-09-03 09:46:37','2026-09-03 09:46:37','2026-09-03 09:46:37'),(1308,5255,5268,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-03 09:54:32','Fetal well-being.','Single live active intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and breech presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is anterior and partly fundal.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nBPD= 50mm,   \r\nEGA = 21 weeks + 0 days, \r\nEDD = 14/01/2027','Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 21 weeks + 0 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-03 09:54:32','2026-09-03 09:54:32','2026-09-03 09:54:32'),(1309,5256,5269,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-03 10:20:04','Thyroid disease','Both thyroid lobes were examined using high resolution transducer. They are both enlarged measuring 39 x 33 x 22mm and 37 x 21 x 11mm in their craniocaudal, mediolateral and AP dimensions on the right and left sides respectively equivalent to about 22mls. The showed heterogeneous parenchymal echotexture and reduction in parenchymal echogenicity. The isthmus is within normal limits.  No calcification or cysts seen within them. The thyroid capsule is preserved.  \r\nThe adjacent great vessels of the neck and  the overlying strap muscles are within normal limits. No lymphadenopathy demonstrated.','Diffuse bilateral thyroid enlargement with ben