hin normal limits.','Early viable intrauterine cyesis at about 10weeks + 2days','completed','2026-09-04 09:59:56','2026-09-04 09:59:56','2026-09-04 09:59:56'),(1353,5299,5312,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 10:09:41',NULL,'The liver is shrunken, measures about 104mm in span. It however showed coarsening of its parenchymal echotexture with increased parenchymal echogenicity and marginal irregularity. However, no focal mass lesion is seen.  The   biliary ducts are not dilated. The gall bladder is demonstrated and show normal outline. \r\nThe spleen is enlarged measuring about 160mm in span but show normal parenchymal echopattern.\r\nThe pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nThe bowel loops however show normal caliber and outline. Mild ascites is noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or lymphadenopathy is seen.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions outline and sizes. They both showed good corticomedullary differentiation. \r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and show normal wall thickness and outline.  \r\nThe uterus, adnexae  are within normal limits.','Features suggest chronic liver disease. Further clinical/laboratory evaluation are advised.','completed','2026-09-04 10:09:41','2026-09-04 10:09:41','2026-09-04 10:09:41'),(1354,5300,5313,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 10:14:17','?Enteritis r/o typhoid perforation','The liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal. The gall bladder is show normal outline and wall thickness.  \r\nThe spleen is normal in size  and show normal echopattern. No focal lesion seen within it.\r\nThe pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops show fluid loading with thickened wall and increased peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, lymphadenopathy or free peritoneal fluid collection seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline.','Features are suggestive of bowel inflammatory changes (entero-colitis).','completed','2026-09-04 10:14:17','2026-09-04 10:14:17','2026-09-04 10:14:17'),(1355,5301,5314,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 10:18:11','Fetal well-being.','Single live active intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is anterior and partly fundal.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nBPD= 89mm, FL= 72mm   \r\nEGA = 36weeks + 3days, \r\nEDD = 29/09/2026','Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 36 weeks + 3 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-04 10:18:11','2026-09-04 10:18:11','2026-09-04 10:18:11'),(1356,5302,5315,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 10:30:29',NULL,'The demonstrated bowel loops  are moderately dilated with thickened wall and show no peristalsis. To and fro movement is noted. Mild free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe liver is normal in size and echo pattern. The gall bladder contains clear content with regular wall thickness and outline. \r\nThe pancreas and para-aortic region are within normal limits.  The spleen is normal in size and shows uniform parenchymal echoes and outline.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They also showed normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly distended with clear urine and show normal wall thickness.','Features are suspicious of intestinal obstruction. Plain abdominal x-ray (erect and supine) is advised for further evaluation.','completed','2026-09-04 10:30:29','2026-09-04 10:26:31','2026-09-04 10:30:29'),(1357,5303,5316,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 10:41:15','Abdominal pain','The liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion is demonstrated.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen. However, an umbilical defect measuring about 30mm is noted. Bowel loops are seen herniating through it.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with urine containing internal echoes and show multi-focal areas of mucosal elevation, One of them measures about 9mm. No calculus is demonstrated.','CONCLUSION: Features suggest \r\n1. Non-obstructing umbilical hernia\r\n2. Chronic cystitis (UTI).','completed','2026-09-04 10:41:15','2026-09-04 10:41:15','2026-09-04 10:41:15'),(1358,5306,5319,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 10:49:09','Cyesis ?abortion','The uterus measures about 37mm in widest AP diameter. Small hypoechoic nodule with a bulge is noted in the anterior myometrial wall, measuring about 22 x 16mm. No intracavitary fluid collection is noted. \r\nThe endometrial plate is intact with normal endometrial/myometrial interface. \r\nBoth adnexae are within normal limits. \r\nThe POD is free.','Features suggest \r\n1. Complete abortion.\r\n2. Small subserous myoma','completed','2026-09-04 10:49:09','2026-09-04 10:49:09','2026-09-04 10:49:09'),(1359,5309,5322,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 11:04:38','Fetal well-being.','Triple live active intrauterine fetuses were seen. Longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is anterior on the body.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nAverage BPD= 53mm, FL= 39mm   \r\nEGA = 22 weeks + 2 days, \r\nEDD = 06/01/2027','Triple viable intrauterine gestation at about 22 weeks + 2 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-04 11:04:38','2026-09-04 11:04:38','2026-09-04 11:04:38'),(1360,5308,5321,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 12:07:41',NULL,'TESTICULAR ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\nBoth testicles are demonstrated and are normal positions and sizes, measuring about 10 and 7.8mls, right and left sides respectively. \r\nHowever, the left testicle, and epididymis showed reduced echogenicity with multiple calcific foci as well as extra-testicular fat stranding. Mild clear peri-testicular fluid collection is noted. \r\nThe right testicle, and epididymis showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture.','Differentials of the above findings include;\r\n1. Epididymo-orchitis\r\n2.  Testicular torsion. Testicular doppler uss is suggested for further evaluation.','completed','2026-09-04 12:07:41','2026-09-04 12:07:41','2026-09-04 12:07:41'),(1361,5310,5323,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 12:10:23',NULL,'The liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal. The gall bladder is show normal outline and wall thickness.  \r\nThe spleen is normal in size  and show normal echopattern. No focal lesion seen within it.\r\nThe pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops show fluid loading with thickened wall and increased peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, lymphadenopathy or free peritoneal fluid collection seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline. \r\nThe prostate is within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of bowel inflammatory changes (entero-colitis).','completed','2026-09-04 12:10:23','2026-09-04 12:10:23','2026-09-04 12:10:23'),(1362,5312,5325,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 12:20:43','?Foreign body.','NECK USS\r\nBoth thyroid lobes were examined using high resolution transducer. They are both normal in size  measuring 10 x 15mm and 9 x 12mm in their mediolateral and AP dimensions on the right and left sides respectively. They showed homogeneous  parenchymal echopattern. No focal mass lesion is seen. The isthmus is within normal limits.. The thyroid capsule is preserved.  \r\nThe adjacent great vessels of the neck and  the overlying strap muscles are within normal limits. No lymphadenopathy demonstrated.','Normal examination','completed','2026-09-04 12:20:43','2026-09-04 12:20:43','2026-09-04 12:20:43'),(1363,5311,5324,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 12:25:09',NULL,'SOFT TISSUE NECK\r\nThe normal cervical curvature is preserved. The demonstrated vertebral bodies, disc spaces, pedicles and the posterior elements are within normal limits. The demonstrated air column is normal in caliber and outline.  No para or pre vertebral soft tissue mass  or foreign body seen.','Normal study.','completed','2026-09-04 12:25:09','2026-09-04 12:25:09','2026-09-04 12:25:09'),(1364,5305,5318,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 12:32:22','?PTB r/o CAP','The heart is normal in size and contour. CTR = 65/130.\r\nThe pulmonary vasculature is within normal limits\r\nNo focal lung parenchymal lesion seen. \r\nThe costophrenic angles are free.\r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissues are within normal limits.','Normal examination','completed','2026-09-04 12:32:22','2026-09-04 12:32:22','2026-09-04 12:32:22'),(1365,5313,5326,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-04 12:42:18',NULL,'PELVIC USS\r\nThe uterus measures about 40mm in widest AP diameter. There is a mixed echo collection (about 20mls) in the endometrial cavity suggestive of retained product of conception (RPOC).\r