r. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is mainly fundal.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nBPD= 26mm,   \r\nEGA = 14 weeks + 3 days, \r\nEDD = 08/03/2027','Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 14 weeks + 3 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-10 11:12:47','2026-09-10 11:12:47','2026-09-10 11:12:47'),(1601,5555,5571,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-10 11:20:29',NULL,'The uterus is normal sized measuring about 41mm in widest AP diameter.  The myometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion seen.  The adnexae are within normal limits. The POD contains significant free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder is grossly  intact.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, spleen and pancreas.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen or ascites seen.','Features are suggestive of PID.','completed','2026-09-10 11:20:29','2026-09-10 11:20:29','2026-09-10 11:20:29'),(1602,5556,5572,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-10 11:28:00','?Fibroid','PELVIC USS\r\nThe uterus measures about 67mm in widest AP dimension. It shows distorted myometrial echopattern by an oval hypoechoic mass within the myomtetrium with calcific foci. It measures about 64 x 39mm in size. The endometrium is ill defined. Similar but smaller mass is seen inferior to it.\r\nBoth adnexae appear within normal limits.\r\nThe POD is free.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system,  pancreas and spleen. Both kidneys are normal in size, shape, position  and echopattern. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted. \r\nNo ascites is demonstrated.','Features suggest multiple uterine fibroids.','completed','2026-09-10 11:28:00','2026-09-10 11:28:00','2026-09-10 11:28:00'),(1603,5557,5573,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-10 11:33:36','Fetal well-being.','Single live active intrauterine fetus in longitud