ays GA.\r\nRepeat scan in 2 weeks to confirm fetal viability','completed','2026-09-19 18:47:23','2026-09-19 18:47:23','2026-09-19 18:47:23'),(1954,5919,5937,21,NULL,21,NULL,'2026-09-19 19:10:36',NULL,'The uterus is normal in size measuring 5 cm in AP diameter. There is a fairly oval hypoechoec mass noted in the posterior myometrial wall.  It measures about 33.56 x 33.16 mm in size. No calcification or cystic changes seen within it.  The endometrial plate is distorted.\r\nThere is also a cystic structure noted in the right adnexa. It measures about 23.92 x 27.7 mm in size. No septation or solid seen within the cyst. The left adnexa is free.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It shows regular outline with normal wall thickness.  No calculus or mass is seen.','1. Features suggest uterine myoma\r\n2. Right adnexal cyst','completed','2026-09-19 19:10:36','2026-09-19 19:10:36','2026-09-19 19:10:36'),(1955,5923,5941,21,NULL,21,NULL,'2026-09-19 19:17:28',NULL,'The uterus is normal in size measuring about 48 mm in AP diameter. It is empty and shows uniform myometrial echoes. The endometrial plate is intact. The myometrial-endometrial interface is preserved. The adnexae are within normal limits. No pelvic lesion is demonstrated The POD is empty.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It shows regular outline with normal wall thickness.  No calculus or mass is seen.','Normal examination','completed','2026-09-19 19:17:28','2026-09-19 19:17:28','2026-09-19 19:17:28'),(1956,5922,5940,21,NULL,21,NULL,'2026-09-19 19:31:20',NULL,'Single live intra uterine fetus seen. \r\nIn longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation. \r\nCardiac activity is present and good.\r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate and clear\r\nPlacenta is posterofundal\r\nBPD =93.63 mm     FL= 72.64 mm   \r\nEGA= 37 weeks + 4 days   \r\nEDD= 6/10/2026\r\nThe internal cervical os is closed.','Single live intrauterine gestation at about 37 weeks + 4 days GA.','completed','2026-09-19 19:31:20','2026-09-19 19:31:20','2026-09-19 19:31:20'),(1957,5924,5942,21,NULL,21,NULL,'2026-09-19 20:04:10',NULL,'Single live intra uterine fetus seen. \r\nIn longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation. \r\nCardiac activity is present and good.\r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate and clear\r\nPlacenta is posterofundal.\r\nBPD =45.37 mm     FL= 29.98 mm   \r\nEGA= 19 weeks + 2 days   \r\nEDD= 11/02/2026\r\nThe internal cervical os is closed.','Single live intrauterine gestation at about 19 weeks + 2 days GA.','completed','2026-09-19 20:04:10','2026-09-19 20:04:10','2026-09-19 20:04:10'),(1958,5927,5945,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 13:57:56','? cyesiss','OBSTETRIC USS\r\nBulky uterus containing a moderate endometrial collection with double decidual reaction suggestive of gestational sac.  No fetal pole or yolk sac is noted.\r\nGSD= 16mm   \r\nEGA= 5 weeks + 6 days \r\nEDD= 17/05/2027\r\nInternal os is closed.   \r\nBoth adnexae and POD appear within normal limits.','Early ?viable intrauterine cyesis at about 5 weeks + 6 days GA. Repeat scan in two weeks or TVS now advised for further evaluation.','completed','2026-09-20 13:57:56','2026-09-20 13:57:56','2026-09-20 13:57:56'),(1959,5926,5944,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 14:12:07','? Cyesis','The uterus is bulky measuring 58mm its widest AP diameter.\r\nThe endometrium contains mixed echo collection about 14ml in volume. \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform.\r\nBoth adnexae are free. \r\nThe POD is empty.\r\nThe urinary bladder is within normal limits.\r\nNil else of note','Features consistent with incomplete abortion.','completed','2026-09-20 14:12:07','2026-09-20 14:12:07','2026-09-20 14:12:07'),(1960,5925,5943,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 14:31:44','? Endometritis','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe uterus is empty measuring about 49 mm in its widest AP diameter.  The myometrial and endometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion or collection seen. A thick wall cystic lesion with internal septations is noted in the right adnexium suggestive of ovarian cyst. No solid component or calcification is noted. The left adnexium is within normal limits. The POD contains mild free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Features suggest right ovarian cyst? haemorraghic.','completed','2026-09-20 14:31:44','2026-09-20 14:31:44','2026-09-20 14:31:44'),(1961,5929,5947,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 15:09:38','? Cystitis.','Abdominal Us\r\nThe liver is normal in size and showed homogenous echopattern. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gallbladder, pancreas and spleen are within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They both showed normal echopattern with good cortico-medullary differentiation and central sinus echoes are preserved. \r\nThe bowel loops are prominent and show fluid loading most especially in the lower abdomen with thickened wall. They are however normal in wall thickness and outline with regular peristalsis. Appendix bed is free.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with urine that shows internal echoes. It shows regular wall outline with increased thickness.','Conclusion;   Features are suggestive of enteritis with cystitis.','completed','2026-09-20 15:09:38','2026-09-20 15:09:38','2026-09-20 15:09:38'),(1962,5931,5949,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 15:27:11','? Right ovarian cyst','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe uterus is bulky measuring about 70 mm in its widest AP diameter.  A hypoechoic lesion is noted in posterior myometrium suggestive of myoma. It measures 38x35mm in size. The endometrial echoes are normal. No collection is seen. The adnexae are within normal limits. The POD contains mild free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Features suggestive of intra-mural myoma.','completed','2026-09-20 15:27:11','2026-09-20 15:25:38','2026-09-20 15:27:11'),(1963,5930,5948,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 15:37:27','? enteric fever','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is normal sized and showed   normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal.  \r\nThe spleen, pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops  in the lower abdomen using high frequency probe showed moderate fluid loading and slightly increased peristalsis. The wall thickness is increased.  No intra-abdominal mass lesion. Mild free peritoneal fluid collection seen.\r\n The urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline. Normal prostate. The left inguinal canal is dilated with bowel loops seen within it. the bowels however, show normal caliber and peristalsis. The right inguinal region is free.','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of enterocolitis with unobstructed left inguinal hernia.','completed','2026-09-20 15:37:27','2026-09-20 15:37:27','2026-09-20 15:37:27'),(1964,5932,5950,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 15:56:28','? Fetal well-being','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nSingle live active  intrauterine fetus. \r\nLongitudinal lie and cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is good.\r\nPlacenta is posterior.  \r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate in volume and clear.\r\nBPD= 42 mm, FL=30 mm   \r\nEGA= 18 weeks+5 days. EDD= 16/02/2027.\r\ninternal os is closed.','Single viable fetus at 18 weeks+5 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-09-20 15:56:28','2026-09-20 15:56:28','2026-09-20 15:56:28'),(1965,5928,5946,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-09-20 15:59:05','? Pylonephritis','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe prostate is normal in size and echopattern.\r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They show reduced echogenicity with effaced sinus echoes and mild calyectasis. The cortico-medullary differentiation is preserved. No calculus is noted.\r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Features suggest bilateral pyelonephritis.','completed','2026-09-20 15:59:05','2026-09-20 15:59:05','2026-09-20 15:59:05'),(1966,5934,5952,21,NULL,21,NULL,'2026-09-20 18:26:55',NULL,'Single live intra uterine fetus seen. \r\nIn transverse lie\r\nCardiac activity is present and good.\r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate and clear\r\nPlacenta is anterior on the uterine body.\r\nBPD =91 mm     FL= 70 mm   \r\nEGA= 18 weeks + 1 day   \r\nEDD= 20/02/2027\r\nThe internal cervical os is closed.','Single live intrauterine gestation at about 18 weeks + 1 day GA.','completed','2026-09-20 18:26:55','2026-09-20 18:26:55','2026-09-20 18:26:55'),(1967,5933,5951,21,NULL,21,NULL,'2026-09-20 18:45:59',NULL,'The lesion was scanned using high frequency transducer. It shows a hypoechoic  collection noted in the subcutaneous region of the forehead.  The overlying skin is within normal limit.','A forehead Haematoma \r\nSkull x ray is recommended','completed','2026-09-20 18:45:59','2026-09-20 18:45:59','2026-09-20 18:45:59'),(1968,5935,5953,21,