ze (about 33mm in widest AP diameter), empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It shows an intact endometrial plate echo.  No intracavitary collection is seen. Both adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of left-side pyelonephritis.','completed','2026-09-25 14:19:22','2026-09-25 14:19:22','2026-09-25 14:19:22'),(2173,6144,6163,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-25 14:25:22',NULL,'Allowing for patient rotation; there is cardiomegaly. CTR=77/130.\r\nThe aorta is unfolded. \r\nThe central vessels are engorged with features of upper lobe blood diversion. \r\nStreaky opacities noted in the  lower lung bases bilaterally with right  pleural effusion. \r\nThe horizontal fissure is thickened.\r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissue are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of congestive cardiac failure. \r\nCVS examination and Echocardiography advised for further evaluation.','completed','2026-09-25 14:25:22','2026-09-25 14:25:22','2026-09-25 14:25:22'),(2174,6150,6169,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-25 14:35:35',NULL,'Normal hepatobiliary system, the spleen, pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in positions, outlines, and shapes. They measure about 83mm and 170mm in bipolar length on the right and left sides respectively. The left show severe pelvicalyceal dilatation with thinning of the renal parenchyma. The cortico-medullary differentiation is good on the right side.  No calculus, cysts or masses seen.\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion or collection seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It showed normal wall thickness and outline. No calculus seen.','Left side severe hydronephrosis? Cause ?r/o PUJ obstruction.\r\nAbdominal CT may be considered for further evaluation.','completed','2026-09-25 14:35:35','2026-09-25 14:35:35','2026-09-25 14:35:35'),(2175,6151,6170,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-09-25 14:56:05','?Right sided breast lump','BREAST ULTRASOUND\r\nThe right