atures are suggestive of Enteritis with PUD.\r\n                      Further Laboratory findings are advised.','completed','2026-09-29 09:09:33','2026-09-29 09:09:33','2026-09-29 09:09:33'),(2343,6320,6339,17,NULL,17,NULL,'2026-09-29 09:13:17',NULL,'There is an extensive homogenous opacity seen involving the entire right lung field due to gross pleural fluid collection. Moderate shifting of the mediastinum is noted. The left lung field showed reticulonudler opacities. \r\nThe heart is obscured by the aforementioned opacity. \r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadow.','Conclusion: Gross Right Sided Pleural Fluid Collection most probably due to the clinically suspected PTB. \r\n                   FBC, ESR, and sputum AFB are advised.','completed','2026-09-29 09:13:17','2026-09-29 09:13:17','2026-09-29 09:13:17'),(2344,6329,6348,17,NULL,17,NULL,'2026-09-29 09:14:46',NULL,'The heart is normal in size and contour CTR = 6.5/12.5\r\nThe aorta is unfolded.\r\nThere are early features of upper lobe blood diversion. \r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissues','Conclusion; Features are those of Hypertensive Heart Disease in Incipient Failure.','completed','2026-09-29 09:14:46','2026-09-29 09:14:46','2026-09-29 09:14:46'),(2345,6328,6347,17,NULL,17,NULL,'2026-09-29 09:16:40',NULL,'There is straightening of the normal lumbar lordosis presumably due to muscle spasm from pain.\r\nThe demonstrated lumbar vertebral bodies, disc spaces, pedicles and the posterior elements are within normal limits \r\nThe visualized facets joints are also within normal limits.','Conclusion;  Lumbar Spinal Straightening? Due to muscle spasm from pain','completed','2026-09-29 09:16:40','2026-09-29 09:16:40','2026-09-29 09:16:40'),(2346,6326,6345,17,NULL,17,NULL,'2026-09-29 09:20:17',NULL,'There is gross hepatomegaly with the liver seen about 8cm below the costal margin. It’s seen enlarging to the left side to displace and compress the stomach and the spleen. It showed gross coarsen