 + 41 day GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-10-03 19:16:20','2026-10-03 19:16:20','2026-10-03 19:16:20'),(2568,6576,6595,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-03 19:31:18','PID R/O FIBROID','The gallbladder is filled and distended with clear bile. It contains an echogenic structures casting posterior acoustic shadowing in its dependent aspect measuring about 17mm in size, The extra and intra-hepatic biliary channels are not dilated. \r\nThe liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal focal mass lesion or collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size and empty measuring about 49.98mm in AP diameter. The endomtrial plate is intact about 32mm in thickness. The myometrial echoes are uniform. No intra-cavitory  collection, gestational sac or focal mass lesion seen. \r\nThe adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of non-obstructing cholelithiasis.','completed','2026-10-03 19:31:18','2026-10-03 19:31:18','2026-10-03 19:31:18'),(2569,6577,6596,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-03 19:44:18','Mastitis r/o tumor','Both breasts were examined using a 7.5MHz transducer. \r\nThey showed normal fibroglandular parenchymal and stromal echoes. No focal breast mass lesion or collection seen.  \r\nThe ductal system is also within normal limits.    \r\nThe retroareolar, retromammary areas and the axillary tails