ing multiple internal mobile echoes and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features are suggestive of cystitis as component of UTI.','completed','2026-10-03 20:14:30','2026-10-03 20:07:23','2026-10-03 20:14:30'),(2572,6582,6601,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-03 21:00:26','BPP/EFW','Single live intrauterine fetus  \r\nIn oblique lie, cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear AFI (58.89mm) \r\nPlacenta is anterior fundal.  \r\nBPD= 94.29mm, FL= 80.85mm, AC = 350.04mm, HC= 352.12mm all corresponding to an average GA of \r\n39 weeks + 6 days 	EDD= 04/10/2026	  EFW = 3.9kg\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2 \r\nTotal =  8/8','Single live intrauterine fetus at about 39 weeks + 6 days GA with satisfactory biophysical profile score.','completed','2026-10-03 21:00:26','2026-10-03 21:00:26','2026-10-03 21:00:26'),(2573,6583,6602,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-04 08:48:55','? UTI','The demonstrated bowel loops especially in lower abdomen are prominent and fluid especially showing thickened wall and increased peristalsis. No focal mass lesion seen. \r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features are suggestive of inflammatory bowel changes presumably enteritis.','completed','2026-10-04 08:48:55','2026-10-04 08:48:55','2026-10-04 08:48:55'),(2574,6584,6603,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-04 08:57:37','?','The liver is normal in size and show regular outline with normal parenchymal echotexture and echogenicity. The intra hepatic veins and biliary ducts are not dilated. No focal hepatic lesion demonstrated.\r\nThe spleen, pancreas and para-aortic area are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and sizes. They showed good cortico-medullary differentiation. No calculus seen. The ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are fluid loaded and showed exaggerated peristalsis with normal caliber presumably due to inflammatory changes. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites seen. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and shows regular outline with normal wall thickness. No mass lesion or calculus seen. No mass lesion or calculus seen.\r\nThe uterus, adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of inflammatory bowel changes presumably enteritis.','completed','2026-10-04 08:57:37','2026-10-04 08:57:37','2026-10-04 08:57:37'),(2575,6585,6604,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-04 09:10:03','?cyesis','The uterus is normal in size measuring about 43mm in AP diameter. It contains an irregular elongated gestational sac with poor decidual reaction in the lower endometrial region and non demonstration of fetal pole.\r\nGSD = 21.62, EGA = 6 Weeks + 3 days \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform. \r\nThe adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is also within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of incomplete abortion','completed','2026-10-04 09:10:03','2026-10-04 09:10:03','2026-10-04 09:10:03'),(2576,6586,6605,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-04 09:33:10','obstetric scan','Twin viable fetuses seen. Both re actively changing positions currently.\r\nString sign is noted.\r\nPlacentas is posterior-fundal on the uterus.  \r\nAmniotic fluid volume is clear and adequate.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular.\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. The internal os is closed.\r\nAveragely: FL = 15.21 mm.     BPD =25.92 mm        \r\nEGA= 14 weeks + 3days                            \r\nEDD= 01/04/2027\r\nSatisfactory gross fetal movement, fine tone and amniotic fluid volume noted. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline and wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Twin viable gestation at about 14 weeks + 3 days GA in satisfactory state.','completed','2026-10-04 09:33:10','2026-10-04 09:33:10','2026-10-04 09:33:10'),(2577,6587,6606,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-04 09:36:59','ENTERITIS','The demonstrated bowel loops are prominent and fluid especially in the left flanks. Multiple enlarged mesenteric lymph nodes are noted. \r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features are suggestive of inflammatory bowel changes presumably enteritis with multiple mesenteric adenopathy? reactionary.','completed','2026-10-04 09:36:59','2026-10-04 09:36:59','2026-10-04 09:36:59'),(2578,6588,6607,5,NULL,5,NULL,'2026-10-04 09:44:59','FWB','Single live intrauterine fetus, in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular,\r\nAdequate liquor