ver is normal in size, measures about 135mm in span. It however showed coarsening of its parenchymal echotexture with increased parenchymal echogenicity. No focal parenchymal lesion is seen. The biliary ducts are not dilated. The gall bladder is demonstrated and show normal outline. The pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits. The spleen is within normal limits.\r\nSevere ascites is noted. The bowel loops however show normal caliber and outline.No intra-bdominal mass lesion or lymphadenopathy demonstrated currently.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions outline and sizes. They both showed good corticomedullary differentiation. \r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and show normal wall thickness and outline.  \r\nThe uterus, and adnexae  are within normal limits.','Features are suspicious of chronic liver disease with severe ascites. Further clinical/laboratory evaluation is advised','completed','2026-10-05 15:39:00','2026-10-05 15:31:48','2026-10-05 15:39:00'),(2673,6685,6704,18,NULL,18,NULL,'2026-10-05 15:41:45','PID r/o UTI','The liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 35.5 mm in its widest AP diameter. It shows intact endometrial plate.  No intracavitary collection focal lesion is seen. \r\