ated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and shows regular outline with normal wall thickness. No mass lesion or calculus seen. No mass lesion or calculus seen.','Features are suggestive of entero-colitis.','completed','2026-10-08 12:33:47','2026-10-08 12:33:47','2026-10-08 12:33:47'),(2792,6812,6831,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-10-08 12:35:58','cyesis','Single live intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently. `\r\ncardiac activity is present and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. 	\r\nPlacenta is anterior on the uterine body. No subchorionic collection seen.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear.\r\nBPD = 77mm, FL = 58mm\r\nEGA= 30 weeks + 2 days, \r\nEDD = 15/12/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 30 weeks + 2 days,  GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-10-08 12:35:58','2026-10-08 12:35:58','2026-10-08 12:35:58'),(2793,6811,6830,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-10-08 12:40:21','cyesis','Twin intra uterine fetuses are demonstrated.\r\nBoth in longitudinal lie but breech presentation currently.  \r\nTwo placentae are noted on the anterior and posterior uterine body.\r\nThe liquor volume is adequate with a dividing membrane (string sign)\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly seen. Internal os is closed.\r\nAverage BPD= 53.5 mm, FL= 35.3 mm, \r\nEGA= 21 weeks + 4 days. EDD= 14/02/27','Twin viable intrauterine fetuses at about 21 weeks + 4 days GA (Dichorionic and diamniotic) in a satisfactory wellbeing.','completed','2026-10-08 12:40:21','2026-10-08 12:40:21','2026-10-08 12:40:21'),(2794,6825,6844,9,NULL,9,NULL,'2026-10-08 13:06:06','?incomplete abortion','The uterus is bulky measuring about 67mm in its widest AP diameter.  The endometrium is thickened, expanded and shows mixed-echogenic material (6.9ml) within it suggestive of retained products of conception. The myometrial echoes are uniform. The internal cervical os is closed. \r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\