hic findings.','completed','2026-10-28 18:58:38','2026-10-28 18:58:38','2026-10-28 18:58:38'),(3854,7950,7972,14,NULL,14,NULL,'2026-10-28 19:11:02','Acute abdomen','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThere is moderate bowel gas shadow demonstrated in the central abdomen. The bowel loops in the lower abdomen and both flanks appear severe dilated with poor peristaltic activity. Significant turbid free intra-peritoneal fluid was demonstrated in the entire abdominal quadrant. Moderate probe pressure tenderness is noted over the abdomen due to peritonitis.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and shows regular outline. The demonstrated prostate is within normal limits.\r\nThe liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echotexture and echogenicity. No focal intrahepatic lesion demonstrated. The gallbladder and spleen are within normal limits. The pancreas and para aortic area are obscured by overlying bowel gas shadows.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in positions, outlines, shapes and sizes.  They show normal parenchymal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No renal mass, calculus or hydronephrosis is seen.','Overall features are suggestive of bowel perforation with multi organs inflammatory changes and peritonitis. \r\nPlain abdominal x-ray erect and supine may be suggested for further evaluation.','completed','2026-10-28 19:11:02','2026-10-28 19:11:02','2026-10-28 19:11:02'),(3855,7954,7976,14,NULL,14,NULL,'2026-10-28 19:12:46','LAP','ABDOMINO-PELVIC ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\n\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits. No intra-abdominal or collection seen. The liver is normal in size and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intra hepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echo pattern. The pancreas is also normal in size and echo pattern.  The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. The uterus is normal in size and showed uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. No cyesis seen. The adnexae and POD re free.','Essentially normal sonographic findings. The possibility of PUD cannot be rule out.','completed','2026-10-28 19:12:46','2026-10-28 19:12:46','2026-10-28 19:12:46'),(3856,7952,7974,14,NULL,14,NULL,'2026-10-28 19:18:41','ABDOMINAL USS','Abdominal USS\r\n\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes 101 and 106 mm in bipolar length on the right and left side respectively. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally. No calculus or hydronephrosis seen.\r\nThe liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intra hepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echo pattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echo pattern.  The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.\r\nThe prostate appears within normal limits.','Essentially normal examination. The possibility of PUD/GERD cannot be rule out. Further evaluations suggested.','completed','2026-10-28 19:18:41','2026-10-28 19:18:41','2026-10-28 19:18:41'),(3857,7951,7973,14,NULL,14,NULL,'2026-10-28 19:23:19','?UTI','Abdominal USS\r\n\r\nT