D= 73 mm, FL=53mm   \r\nEGA= 29 weeks+4 days. EDD=   11/01/2027.','Single viable fetus at 29 weeks+4 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','completed','2026-10-30 14:31:10','2026-10-30 14:31:10','2026-10-30 14:31:10'),(3956,8056,8079,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 14:35:07',NULL,'LUMBOSACRAL SPINE\r\nThere is straightening of the normal lumbar lordosis.\r\nAnterior marginal osteophytes are noted on the vertebrae. The demonstrated vertebral bodies are normal in density and height.\r\n The intervening disc spaces, pedicles and posterior elements are within normal limits. \r\nNormal para-vertebral soft tissue shadow','Conclusion: Features suggest lumbar spondylosis.','completed','2026-10-30 14:35:07','2026-10-30 14:35:07','2026-10-30 14:35:07'),(3957,8060,8083,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 14:42:37','? Fetal well-being','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nSingle live active  intrauterine fetus. \r\nLongitudinal lie and cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is good.\r\nPlacenta is anterior.  \r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate in volume and clear.\r\nBPD= 32 mm, FL=18mm   \r\nEGA= 16 weeks. EDD= 16/04/2027.\r\ninternal os is closed.\r\nThe bowel loops are fluid loaded with thickened wall and increased peristalsis. nil ascites. \r\nNormal hepatobiliary system. spleen, pancreas and kidneys.','1. Single viable fetus at 16 weeks GA in satisfactory well-being.\r\n2. Enteritis (maternal).','completed','2026-10-30 14:42:37','2026-10-30 14:42:37','2026-10-30 14:42:37'),(3958,8061,8084,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 14:48:57','?','Abdominal Us\r\nThe liver is normal in size and showed homogenous echopattern. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gallbladder, pancreas and spleen are within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They both showed normal echopattern with good cortico-medullary differentiation and central sinus echoes are preserved. \r\nThe bowel loops are prominent and show fluid loading most especially in the lower abdomen with thickened wall. They are however normal in caliber and outline with regular peristalsis.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with urine that shows internal echoes. It shows regular wall outline with increased thickness. Normal prostate.','Conclusion;   Features are suggestive of enteritis with cystitis.','completed','2026-10-30 14:48:57','2026-10-30 14:48:57','2026-10-30 14:48:57'),(3959,8062,8085,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 15:01:59','? PCOS','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe uterus is empty measuring about 37 mm in its widest AP diameter.  The myometrial and endometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion or collection seen. The adnexae are within normal limits. The left ovary is normal in size about 6.2ml in volume. It shows normal follicular echopattern. The POD is free.\r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Normal examination.','completed','2026-10-30 15:01:59','2026-10-30 15:01:59','2026-10-30 15:01:59'),(3960,8063,8086,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 15:12:37','? Early cyesis','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe uterus is empty measuring about 39 mm in its widest AP diameter.  Moderate endometrial collection is noted. The myometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion or collection seen. No decidual reaction is noted. The adnexae are within normal limits. The POD contains mild free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Minimal endometrial collection ?PID? early cyesis. Repeat scan in two weeks advised.','completed','2026-10-30 15:12:37','2026-10-30 15:12:37','2026-10-30 15:12:37'),(3961,8026,8049,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 15:20:08','ABDOMINAL SWELLING','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is mildly enlarged about 168mm in span.  It showed  normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic veins are dilated and seen draining into dilated IVC. The biliary systems are normal. No focal mass lesion is seen. \r\nThe spleen, pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops  in the lower abdomen using high frequency probe showed moderate fluid loading and slightly increased peristalsis. The wall thickness is increased.  No intra-abdominal mass lesion. No free peritoneal fluid collection seen. Epigastric probe tenderness elicited? PUD.\r\n The urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline. Normal uterus and adnexae.','Conclusion:  1. Features are suggestive of congestive hepatomegaly? cardiac.\r\n                     2. Enteritis with PUD.','completed','2026-10-30 15:20:08','2026-10-30 15:20:08','2026-10-30 15:20:08'),(3962,8064,8087,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 15:29:10','? Incomplete abortion','The uterus is normal in size and empty measuring 40mm its widest AP diameter.\r\nThe endometrial plate is intact. No cyesis or RPOC demonstrated.\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform.\r\nBoth adnexae are free. \r\nThe POD is empty.\r\nThe urinary bladder is within normal limits.\r\nNil else of note','Features consistent with complete abortion.','completed','2026-10-30 15:29:10','2026-10-30 15:29:10','2026-10-30 15:29:10'),(3963,8065,8088,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 15:31:15','?ccf','CHEST\r\nThere are perihilar and paracardial patchy opacities demonstrated bilaterally more marked on the right. The costophrenic angles appear free. \r\nThe heart is normal in size and contour, CTR=0.45.  \r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of bronchopneumonia.','completed','2026-10-30 15:31:15','2026-10-30 15:31:15','2026-10-30 15:31:15'),(3964,8066,8089,6,NULL,6,NULL,'2026-10-30 15:44:38','?','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is normal sized and showed  normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal. No focal mass lesion is seen. \r\nThe spleen, pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops  in the lower abdomen using high frequency probe showed moderate fluid loading and slightly increased peristalsis. The wall thickness is increased.  No intra-abdominal mass lesion. Mild free peritoneal fluid collection seen.\r\n The urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline. Normal uterus and adnexae.','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of enterocolitis.','completed','2026-10-30 15:44:38','2026-10-30 15:44:38','2026-10-30 15:44:38'),(3965,8067,8090,12,NULL,12,NULL,'2026-10-30 18:18:33','OBSTETRIC USS (BPP+EFW)','Single live intrauterine fetus is seen  in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is good.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate and clear with AFI of 5.1cm\r\nPlacenta is anterofundal\r\nFL=76.7mm, AC=346.6mm, \r\nAverage EGA=39weeks+1day, \r\nAverage EDD=05/11/2026\r\nEFW=3.7Kg\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen\r\nBPP SCORE\r\nFetal gross movement=2, Fetal tone=2, AFI=2, Fetal respiratory excursions=2\r\nTotal score=8/8\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform and internal os is closed','Single live intrauterine gestation at 39weeks+1day GA  with satisfactory BPP scores','completed','2026-10-30 18:18:33','2026-10-30 18:18:33','2026-10-30 18:18:33'),(3966,8068,8091,12,NULL,12,NULL,'2026-10-30 18:23:03','ABDOMINOPELVIC USS','The liver is normal in size and outline. It showed normal parenchymal echotexture and echo reflectivity. The hepatic veins are within normal limits. No focal hepatic parenchymal lesion is seen.\r\nThe gall bladder is filled with clear bile. It showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen. The biliary ducts are normal in caliber and luminal echoes.\r\nThe spleen is mildly enlarged with a span of 136mm. It showed regular outline, normal parenchymal echotexture and echoreflectivtiy. No focal parenchymal lesion is seen.\r\nThe pancreas is also normal in size and parenchymal echo pattern. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, ascites or adenopathy is seen. The region of the appendix is within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They showed normal echo pattern with good corticomedullary differentiation. No mass lesion or calculus is seen. The collecting system and ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is filled with clear urine and showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe prostate gland is normal in size, outline and echo pattern. No focal lesion is seen.','Mild splenomegaly. Further clinical evaluation is advised','completed','2026-10-30 18:23:03','2026-10-30 18:23:03','2026-10-30 18:23:03'),(3967,8069,8092,12,NULL,12,NULL,'2026-10-30 18:26:13','ABDOMINOPELVIC USS','The liver is normal in size and outline. It showed normal parenchymal echotexture and echo reflectivity. The hepatic veins are within normal limits. No focal hepatic parenchymal lesion is 