INSERT INTO `result_templates` VALUES (1,5,'NSW','Abdominal discomfort','The liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus, adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Essentially normal examination','2026-08-02 17:08:50','2026-08-02 17:08:50'),(2,5,'OBS NORMAL','MALARIA R/O UTI','Single live intrauterine fetus, in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation currently.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular,\r\nAdequate liquor volume,\r\nPlacenta is anterior on the body.\r\nBPD = 88mm, FL = 72.3mm,\r\nEGA = 36 Weeks + 1 days,\r\nEDD = 29/08/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine fetus at about 36 weeks + 1 day GA','2026-08-02 17:48:04','2026-08-02 17:48:04'),(3,5,'ABD USS PELVIC HEMATOMA','Lower abdominal pain','There is multi-loculated heterogeneous mass lesion predominantly hypo-echoic with lobulated outline in the pelvic cavity seen occupying the both adnexae and POD. It bears medium level echoes with multiple sepatations. The largest pocket measures about 75x46mm in size. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 34mm in widest AP diameter. It shows an intact endometrial plate echo.  No intracavitary collection or gestational sac is seen. \r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Features suggest pelvic cavity collection?? Hematoma.\r\nSerum PT is suggested to r/o ruptured ectopic.\r\n\r\nDRs. AMINU MB/ABDURRAHMAN Y.','2026-08-02 18:29:29','2026-08-02 18:29:29'),(4,5,'Pelvic incomplete abortion','Incomplete abortion','The uterus is bulky measuring about 55mm in AP diameter. It contains heterogeneous structures about 7.39ml in volume suggestive of product of conception. \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform. \r\nThe adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is also within normal limits.','Incomplete abortion','2026-08-02 18:37:17','2026-08-02 18:37:17'),(5,5,'Obs transverse lie','Fetal well-being','Single live intrauterine fetus, in transverse lie with fetal head to the right maternal spine side currently.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular,\r\nAdequate liquor volume,\r\nPlacenta is posterior on the body.\r\nBPD =30.3mm, FL = 23mm,\r\nEGA = 15 Weeks + 6 days,\r\nEDD = 18/01/2027\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Single viable intrauterine fetus at about 15 weeks + 6 day GA in satisfactory well-being.','2026-08-02 18:42:26','2026-08-02 18:42:26'),(6,5,'NSW updated','Lower abdominal pain','The liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size and empty measuring about 34mm in AP diameter. The endomtrial plate is intact about 2mm in thickness. The myometrial echoes are uniform. No intra-cavitory  collection, gestational sac or focal mass lesion seen. \r\nThe adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Essentially normal examination','2026-08-02 19:26:23','2026-08-02 19:26:23'),(7,6,'Obs NS','? Fetal well-being','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nSingle live active  intrauterine fetus. \r\nLongitudinal lie and cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is good.\r\nPlacenta is posterior.  \r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate in volume and clear.\r\nBPD= 58 mm, FL=42mm   \r\nEGA= 23 weeks+6days. EDD=   25/11/2026.','Single viable fetus at 23 weeks+6days GA in satisfactory well-being.','2026-08-03 08:36:26','2026-08-03 08:59:36'),(8,6,'obs Breech','? Gestational age','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nSingle live,  active intrauterine fetus. Currently breech.\r\nCardiac activity is good. Fetal gross body movements and reflexes are normal.\r\nLiquor volume is clear and adequate. \r\nPlacenta is posterior in the body.\r\nBPD= 49 mm, FL = 30mm   GA= 20 weeks EDD= 21/12/2026.','Single viable fetus at about  20 weeks GA in satisfacatory well-being.','2026-08-03 08:51:46','2026-08-03 08:51:46'),(9,6,'obs BPP, Placenta','?BPP, fetal weight and placentation','Single live intrauterine fetus is demonstrated.  \r\nIn longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear AFV (6.2 x 5.0 cm) \r\nPlacenta is posterior on the body. No retroplacental haemorrage is noted. A focal hypoechoic lesion is noted in posterior aspect of the placenta measuring about 72x63mm in size. No calcification is noted. ? significance.  \r\nBPD= 76mm, FL= 59mm, AC = 268mm, HC= 271mm all corresponding to an average GA of 30weeks + 2days 	EDD= 10/10/2026	  EFW = 1709g\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2','Single live intrauterine fetus at about 30weeks + 2 days GA with satisfactory biophysical profile score. Obstetric Doppler or Follow up scan advised.','2026-08-03 09:18:50','2026-08-03 09:18:50'),(10,6,'ABD F PID','? PID','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe uterus is empty measuring about 49 mm in its widest AP diameter.  The myometrial and endometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion or collection seen. The adnexae are within normal limits. The POD contains mild free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Minimal POD collection ?PID.','2026-08-03 09:40:22','2026-08-03 09:40:22'),(11,6,'pelvic NS','? Cyesis','The uterus is normal in size and empty measuring 35mm its widest AP diameter.\r\nThe endometrial plate is intact. No cyesis or RPOC demonstrated.\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform.\r\nBoth adnexae are free. \r\nThe POD is empty.\r\nThe urinary bladder is within normal limits.\r\nNil else of note','Essentially normal examination.','2026-08-03 09:51:38','2026-08-03 09:51:38'),(12,6,'abd Fpost-partum','?','Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion is seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine. No calculus is demonstrated. It shows normal wall thickness.\r\nThe uterus is bulky measuring about 70mm in AP diameter. The endometrium contains mixed echoes collection about 32ml? lochia. No fetal parts or placental tissue is noted. POD and adnexae are free.','Normal post-partum uterus','2026-08-03 10:16:51','2026-08-03 10:16:51'),(13,6,'obs CRL','? cyesis','OBSTETRIC USS\r\nBulky uterus containing a single intact gestational sac with a live fetal pole\r\nCardiac pulsation is noted. \r\nCRL= 15mm   \r\nEGA= 7weeks + 5days \r\nEDD= 17/03/2027\r\nInternal os is closed.   \r\nBoth adnexae and POD appear within normal limits.','Early viable intrauterine cyesis at about 7 weeks + 5 days GA in satisfactory well-being.','2026-08-03 10:40:53','2026-08-03 10:40:53'),(14,6,'obs BPP ns','?BPP,','Single live intrauterine fetus is demonstrated.  \r\nIn longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear AFV (4.5 x 4.0 cm) \r\nPlacenta is anterior on the body. No retroplacental haemorrage is noted. \r\nBPD= 88mm, FL= 74mm, AC = 298mm, HC= 308mm all corresponding to an average GA of 38weeks + 2 days 	EDD= 15/08/2026	  EFW = 2873g\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2','Single live intrauterine fetus at about 38weeks + 2 days GA with satisfactory biophysical profile score.','2026-08-03 11:17:08','2026-08-03 11:17:08'),(15,6,'abd obs missed','?','Abdominal Uss.\r\nBulky uterus containing an irregularly shaped gestational sac with an echogenic embryonic pole within it. No cardiac pulsation is noted. Poor decidual reaction is noted. \r\nGSD = 38.1 mm. GA = 8weeks +  4day GA.\r\nBoth adnexae are free. Internal os is closed. \r\nThe POD is within normal limits.\r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine and shows normal wall thickness with regular outline. \r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes.','Features are suggestive of a missed abortion.','2026-08-03 11:25:54','2026-08-03 11:25:54'),(16,6,'abd F Enteritis, cystitis','?','Abdominal Us\r\nThe liver is normal in size and showed homogenous echopattern. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gallbladder, pancreas and spleen are within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They both showed normal echopattern with good cortico-medullary differentiation and central sinus echoes are preserved. \r\nThe bowel loops are prominent and show fluid loading most especially in the lower abdomen with thickened wall. They are however normal in wall thickness and outline with regular peristalsis.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with urine with internal echoes. It shows regular in outline and normal wall thickness.','Conclusion;   Features are suggestive of enteritis with cystitis.','2026-08-03 11:34:57','2026-08-03 11:34:57'),(17,6,'obs EFW',NULL,'OBSTETRICS USS    \r\nSingle live intrauterine fetus is demonstrated in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation. Cardiac activity is good and regular.\r\n Placenta is posterior on the uterine body.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate. \r\nBPD= 85 mm,      FL= 68 mm, HC=320 mm, AC=316 mm.      \r\nEGA= 35 weeks + 1 day, EFW=2.7 KG     \r\nEDD= 06 /09/2026\r\nInternal os is closed.','Single viable cyesis at about 35 weeks + 1 day GA in satisfactory well-being.','2026-08-03 11:51:25','2026-08-03 11:51:25'),(18,6,'obs BPP Post date','?post date','Single live intrauterine fetus is demonstrated.  \r\nIn longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear AFV (9.7 x 8.0 cm) \r\nPlacenta is anterior on the body. No retroplacental haemorrage is noted. \r\nBPD= 95mm, FL= 79mm, AC = 357mm, HC= 333mm all corresponding to an average GA of 40weeks + 3 days 	EDD= 31/07/2026	  EFW = 3940g\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2','Single live intrauterine post-dated fetus at about 40weeks + 3 days GA with satisfactory biophysical profile score.','2026-08-03 12:02:51','2026-08-03 12:02:51'),(19,6,'abd M enteritis, gastritis','Recurrent abdominal pain and vomitting. Had appendectomy 20 year ago. Dx Acute abdomen ? cause.','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is normal sized and showed   normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal.  \r\nThe spleen, pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops  in the lower abdomen using high frequency probe showed moderate fluid loading and slightly increased peristalsis. The wall thickness is increased.  No intra-abdominal mass lesion. Mild free peritoneal fluid collection seen. The stomach is distended with copius gastric residue with increased wall thickening about 17mm. No intra-luminal mass is noted.\r\n The urinary bladder is mildly distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline.','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of enterocolitis with gastritis. Barium meal is advised.','2026-08-03 12:10:49','2026-08-03 12:10:49'),(20,6,'CXR BPN, Scoliosis','?','CHEST\r\n\r\nAllowing for rotation on the radiograph\r\nThere is an area of inhomogenous radio-opacity with air-bronchogram noted in both lung fields. The costophrenic angles are spared.  \r\nThere is cardiomegaly with left ventricular configuration  CTR 6/11.  \r\nThere is gentle scoliosis with convexity to the left. the remaining bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows are within normal limits.','CONCLUSION: 1. Features are suggestive of bronchopneumonia with hypertensive heart disease.\r\n                         2. Scoliosis? cause.','2026-08-03 18:09:17','2026-08-03 18:09:17'),(21,6,'CXR R Pleural effusion chest tube','Nil','CHEST\r\n\r\nNo previous radiograph(s) for comparison. Allowing for this. The is right mid and  lower zonal  homogenous opacity  with concave    upper border, lamella component  and obliteration of the costophrenic angle and  hemidiaphragm  due to gross  pleural fluid collection. The ipsilateral upper zone is still aerated  The remaining left lung field is clear. The  bony thorax and the overlying soft tissues are within normal limits. Chest tube noted in situ in the right lower lung zone.','Moderate right sided  Pleural fluid collection. Kindly re-evaluate  chest tube function.','2026-08-03 18:18:40','2026-08-03 18:18:40'),(22,6,'ARM missing inplant',NULL,'LEFT ARM\r\nAllowing for metallic artifacts on the radiograph.\r\nThe demonstrated bones, articular margins, joints spaces and the axial relations are within normal limits. A linear tubular metallic density is noted in the posterior medial aspect of the arm. Normal remaining overlying soft tissue shadow.','Features in keeping with intramuscular implanon.','2026-08-03 18:30:24','2026-08-03 18:30:24'),(23,6,'CXR BPN',NULL,'CHEST\r\nThere are perihilar and paracardial patchy opacities demonstrated bilaterally more marked on the right. The costophrenic angles appear free. \r\nThe heart is normal in size and contour, CTR 4.5/11.  \r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows are within normal limits.','Features are suggestive of bronchopneumonia.','2026-08-03 18:34:36','2026-08-03 18:34:36'),(24,6,'LS Spondylosis',NULL,'LUMBOSACRAL SPINE\r\nThere is straightening of the normal lumbar lordosis.\r\nAnterior marginal osteophytes are noted on L2 vertebra . The demonstrated vertebral bodies are normal in density and height.\r\n The intervening disc spaces, pedicles and posterior elements are within normal limits. \r\nNormal para-vertebral soft tissue shadow','Conclusion: Features suggest mild lumbar spondylosis.','2026-08-03 18:38:48','2026-08-03 18:38:48'),(25,6,'CXR NS','nil','CHEST\r\nThe heart is normal in size and contour CTR = 4.5/11.5\r\nThe pulmonary vasculature is within normal limits\r\nNo focal lung parenchymal lesion seen. \r\nThe costophrenic angles are free.\r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissues are within normal limits.','Normal chest examination','2026-08-03 18:42:23','2026-08-03 18:42:23'),(26,6,'ankle osteitis, cellulitis','Pain and swelling','ANKLE\r\nThe ankle mortis is preserved. There is osteopenia involving the tarsal bones. The demonstrated articular margins joints spaces and the axial relations are within normal limits. Overlying soft tissue swelling is noted.','Features suggest osteitis with cellulitis.','2026-08-03 18:50:31','2026-08-03 18:50:31'),(27,6,'skull NS','?','SKULL\r\nThe demonstrated skull vault, sutures and sella are within normal limits. No features to suggest fracture lines seen. Normal overlying soft tissue outline.','Normal examination','2026-08-03 18:57:42','2026-08-03 18:57:42'),(28,6,'CXR HHDx','?','CHEST\r\nThere is cardiomegaly with left ventricular configuration CTR = 55%.\r\nThe aorta is unfolded\r\nThe pulmonary vasculatures are within normal limits.\r\nNo focal lung parenchyma lesion is seen\r\nBoth costophrenic angles are free.\r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows.','Features suggest hypertensive heart disease.','2026-08-03 19:03:20','2026-08-03 19:03:20'),(29,5,'Sub-cutaneous lipoma','Left hypochondrial lipoma','The sub-cuatneous layer is expanded with an iso-echoic oval well-defined margin mass lesion in the left hypochondrial region. It is seen beyond the transducer field of view with an estimated size of about 38x18mm in size. No calcification or collection seen within it. \r\nThe overlying epiderma, dermal and underlying muscles are within normal limits.','Left hypochondrial sub-cutaneous lipoma','2026-08-03 19:51:55','2026-08-03 19:51:55'),(30,5,'Abd uss complex adnexal cyst','Lower abdominal pain','The uterus is normal in size and empty. It measures abut 40mm in its widest AP diameter. The endometrial plate is intact. The myometrial echoes are uniform. No intracavitory collection or focal lesion seen. \r\nThere is a thick-wall fairly oval mass lesion in the right adnexium measuring about 40x38mm in size. It shows low level echoes with internal septations. No calcifications seen within it. The left adnexium and POD are within normal limits.\r\nThe liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echopattern. No focal mass lesion seen. The pancreas is also normal in size and echopattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits.\r\nNo intra-abdominal collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features are suggestive of right complex adnexal cyst.\r\nFollow up scan is suggested after a course of antinbiotics.','2026-08-03 20:02:09','2026-08-03 20:02:09'),(31,5,'OBS BPP NORMAL','BPP/EFW','Single live intrauterine fetus  \r\nIn oblique lie, cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear AFI (10 cm) \r\nPlacenta is anterior fundal.  \r\nBPD= 90.6mm, FL= 76.92mm, AC = 342.1mm, HC= 336.56mm all corresponding to an average GA of \r\n38weeks + 0days 	EDD= 17/08/2026	  EFW = 3.5kg\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2 \r\nTotal =  8/8','Single live intrauterine fetus at about 38weeks  GA with satisfactory biophysical profile score.','2026-08-03 20:18:51','2026-08-03 20:18:51'),(32,8,'NSW',NULL,'The liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echopattern. No focal hepatic mass lesion demonstrated. The intrahepatic veins and biliary ducts are within normal limits. Normal portal vein.\r\nThe gallbladder, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits. The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are normal in calibre and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal collection or mass lesion is seen. The appendiceal bed is within normal limits.\r\nThe uterus is normal in size and shows uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. No intra-cavitary collection cyesis or mass lesion identified. The ovaries are normal in volume and show random distribution of follicles. The POD is empty. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Essentially normal examination','2026-08-04 10:06:22','2026-08-17 12:01:13'),(33,8,'PELVIS USS','Pyelonephritis','The uterus is normal in size and shows uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. \r\nNo intra-cavitary collection cyesis or mass lesion identified.\r\nThe ovaries are normal in volume and shows random follicular distribution. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus or mass lesion is demonstrated.','Essentially normal examination','2026-08-04 10:25:49','2026-08-04 10:25:49'),(34,8,'ILEUS','Abdominal distension','The liver is normal sized   and showed normal parenchymal echopattern. No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic veins and biliary ducts are within normal limits. Normal portal vein.\r\nThe gallbladder, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits. The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are fluid loaded and shows to-and-fro peristalsis. No intra-abdominal collection or mass lesion is seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features suggest intestinal obstruction ?ileus.','2026-08-04 10:32:19','2026-08-04 10:32:19'),(35,8,'Obs actively','Cyesis','OBSTETRICS USS    \r\nSingle live active intrauterine fetus is demonstrated.\r\nActively changing position.\r\nCardiac activity is good and regular.\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is identified.\r\nPlacenta is posterior on the uterine body.\r\nLiquor volume is adequate. \r\nBPD= mm, EGA= weeks + days    EDD= 22/08/2026\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform. \r\nInternal os is closed.','Single viable intra-uterine cyesis at a