e and mucosal wall, no calculus is seen.','Conclusion; Features are suggestive of Enterocolitis with? Peritonitis? Cause. \r\n                      Plain abdominal X-Ray Erect and Supine are suggested to exclude bowel perforation','2026-08-09 12:42:03','2026-08-09 12:42:03'),(137,17,'CHEST NS',NULL,'The heart size is normal in size and contour CTR = 4.5/11\r\nNo focal lung lesion is seen. The costo-phrenic angles are free. \r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissues are within normal limits.','Conclusion: Essential Normal Study Son graphically. Rely on your clinical findings','2026-08-09 12:45:30','2026-08-09 12:45:30'),(138,17,'Abd Uss Enterocolitis',NULL,'The liver is normal in size. No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe gallbladder is normal in caliber and shows regular outline and wall thickness. No calculus is seen. The spleen and the pancreas are also normal in size and echo pattern. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally. \r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops in the abdomen are prominent and showed generalized increased wall thickening with fluid loading and increased peristalsis. \r\nNo free intraperitoneal collection seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is demonstrated and grossly intact.','Conclusion; Features are suggestive of Enterocolitis.	\r\n                         Further laboratory findings are advised','2026-08-09 12:59:43','2026-08-09 12:59:43'),(139,17,'Chest COPD',NULL,'There are reticuler opacities seen bilaterally worse on the right lung side with accentuation of the bronchovascular markings \r\nThe heart is normal sized CTR= 05/12\r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissues are within normal limits.','Conclusion: Features are suggestive of COPD (Chronic Bronchitis) to r/o PTB by non Radio