ormal.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines, shape and sizes. They showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and corticomedullary distinction. However bilateral distortion of the central sinus echoes worse on the left side. No renal calculus is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and is within normal limits. \r\nNo intrabdominal mass lesion or collection seen.  The bowel loops are normal son graphically.\r\nThe prostate is demonstrated and intact.','Conclusion:  Features of Bilateral Renal Inflammatory Changes most probably Pyelonephritis.','2026-08-16 10:33:39','2026-08-16 10:33:39'),(270,17,'Incomplete Abortion GSD',NULL,'The uterus is bulky and contains irregular collapsing gestational sac with no fetal pole within it yet, extending to the lower uterine segment consistent of retent product \r\nGSD= 17.6mm    GA= 06wks +  0days\r\nThe internal os is closed. \r\nBoth adnexae and the POD are free','Conclusion:  Features suggest Incomplete Abortion.','2026-08-16 10:56:01','2026-08-16 10:56:01'),(271,17,'OBS GSD',NULL,'Bulky uterus containing a single intact gestational sac with no fetal pole seen within it yet\r\nGSD= 11.5mm   GA= 05weeks +  1days.\r\nEDD= 17/04/27  \r\nInternal os is closed. \r\nThe urinary bladder is within normal limits.\r\nThe POD is empty.','Conclusion:  Early Intrauterine Cyesis? Viability.\r\n                     A repeat scan is advised in 4 weeks to ascertain viability.','2026-08-16 11:04:29','2026-08-16 11:27:45'),(272,17,'PELVIS AND BOTH HIPS',NULL,'The demonstrated bones are well mineralized. The right hip joint articular surfaces, margins and axial relations are within normal limits. The upper lateral  margin of the left acetabulum shows marginal outgrowths in keeping with early degenerative changes.\r\nNo fracture line demonstrated. No radiographic  evidence of fracture or dislocation seen.','Conclusion; Features are suggestive of Left Hip Osteoarthritis.','2026-08-16 12:10:51','2026-08-16 12:10:51'