ot be demonstrated. There is moderate to severe probe pressure tenderness demonstrated. The remaining demonstrated bowel loops in the central and upper abdomen are thickened, dilated with fluid loading with increase peristalsis. No intra abdominal mass seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and shows regular outline with normal wall thickness. No mass lesion or calculus seen.','Features are suggestive of right iliac fossa tenderness presumably due to acute appendicitis with high suspicion of rupture.\r\nFurther evaluation is advised.','2026-08-23 19:14:17','2026-08-23 19:14:17'),(363,17,'Enteritis with PUD',NULL,'The liver is normal in size. No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intrahepatic and extra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe gallbladder is normal in caliber and shows regular outline and wall thickness. No calculus is seen. The spleen and the pancreas are also normal in size and echo pattern. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally. \r\nNo intra-abdominal mass or collection is seen.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops in the abdomen are prominent and showed generalized increased wall thickness with fluid loading increased peristalsis \r\nThe urinary bladder is within normal limits.\r\nThe uterus, both adnexae and POD are within normal limits','Conclusion; Features are suggestive of Enteritis with PUD\r\n                          Further laboratory findings are advised','2026-08-24 08:24:39','2026-08-24 08:24:39'),(364,17,'Prostate BPH',NULL,'The liver, biliary tree, pancreas and spleen are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outlines and sizes. They show good corticomedullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. No renal calculus but there is back pressure effect seen bilaterally. \r\nNo intrabdomi