ith PID and PUD.','2026-08-24 08:47:26','2026-08-24 08:47:26'),(367,17,'Abdomen Cystitis',NULL,'Normal hepatobiliary system. The spleen, pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits.  \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and sizes. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. No calculus or back pressure demonstrated.\r\nNo focal renal lesion seen.  \r\nNo ascites or intraabdominal mass lesion.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with urine containing mobile internal echoes. No calculus, calcification or sludge seen.\r\nThe prostate is demonstrated and grossly intact.','Conclusion: Features are suggestive of Chronic Cystitis as a component of U.T.I.    \r\n                          Urine M/C/S is advised for further evaluation','2026-08-24 09:07:05','2026-08-24 09:07:05'),(368,17,'OBS Unstable Lie',NULL,'Single, live active intrauterine fetus  \r\nUnstable lie, Cardiac activity is regular. \r\nAmniotic fluid is clear and adequate for age. \r\nPlacental is posterofundal. \r\nBPD= 47.8mm,   FL= 29.3mm    EGA = 19weeks + 0days\r\nEDD= 18/01/27','Conclusion: Single viable fetus at 19weeks GA.','2026-08-24 09:48:41','2026-08-24 09:48:41'),(369,17,'Breast Uss Mass? Malignancy',NULL,'Both breasts were  examined  using a 7.5MHz  transducer. \r\nThere is an heterogeneous hypoechoic solid mass demonstrated in the left breast. This mass occupy the entire left breast shows surrounding architectural distortion. No calcification or cystic changes seen. \r\nNot associated with enlarge lymph nodes are seen \r\nThe right breast is grossly within normal limits.','Conclusion: Features are suggestive of Left Breast Masses with Suspicious of Malignancy\r\n                    Breast Mammography/ Biopsy advised','2026-08-24 10:07:05','2026-08-24 10:07:05'),(370,17,'Abd Uss NSW',NULL,'The liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. T