20:34','2026-08-24 13:20:34'),(382,17,'Neck X-ray Normal',NULL,'There is straightening of the cervical lordosis. \r\nThe demonstrated cervical vertebral bones, disc spaces, air column, prevertebral soft tissue shadows and surrounding soft tissues appear within normal limits.   \r\n No any abnormal opacities object is seen.','Conclusion;   Essentially Normal Examination','2026-08-24 13:33:57','2026-08-24 13:33:57'),(383,15,'Breast (mastitis)','Right breast discomfort and heaviness','BREAST ULTRASOUND                              \r\nBoth breasts were examined using high frequency probes.  Fibroglandular parenchymal and stromal echoes are also demonstrated in both breasts. The right breast showed an area of thickened hypoechoic glandular tissues with equally thickened parenchyma stroma consistent with inflammatory changes. This area is noted in the 11-1\'o\' clock region of the right breast. No calcification. No mixed echo lesion is seen to suggest abscess collection. There is no associated thickening of the overlying skin.  No axillary lymphadenopathy is noted.\r\nBoth breast showed dilated mammary and lactiferous duct with areas of fusiform dilatations converging to the subareolar area  and the nipple more marked on the right breast  consistent with lactating breasts. \r\nThe pectoralis muscles, the  axillary tails and retromammary area showed normal appearances. \r\nThe left breast is within normal limits.','Features suggest right breast mastitis.','2026-08-25 10:29:51','2026-08-25 10:30:16'),(384,15,'Obstetrics uss (Twin gestation)','Cyesis','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nTwin viable fetuses seen. The leading twin is longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation and the 2nd twin is also is transverse lie with the fetal head to the right of the maternal spine.  One Placentae is seen on the anterior-fundal wall of the myometrium.  String sign is noted. Amniotic fluid volume is clear and adequate in the sac of both twin. \r\nCardiac activity are good and regular.\r\nNo gross fetal ano