d. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 32mm in its widest AP diameter. It shows intact endometrial plate.  No intracavitary collection focal lesion is seen. \r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.\r\nComplementary chest x-ray showed the heart normal in size and contour with the apex pointing towards the right side. The discending aorta and The gastric shadow noted on the right while the hepatic shadow on the left. Normal pulmonary parenchyma, bony thorax and overlying soft tissue outline.','Features suggest situs inversus (incidental finding).','2026-08-26 10:44:37','2026-08-26 10:44:37'),(387,18,'Obst twin',NULL,'Twin viable intra uterine fetuses seen\r\nBoth in longitudinal lie, breech presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is good. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly seen. \r\nPlacenta is anterior on the body.\r\nAmniotic fluid is adequate. \r\nAVERAGE BPD = 48mm, FL = 30mm \r\nAGA=19weeks + 6days.         			\r\nEDD=14/01/2027','Twin viable intrauterine fetuses at about 19weeks  + 6days GA in satisfactory well-being.','2026-08-26 11:20:48','2026-08-26 11:20:48'),(388,18,'Hepato-splenomegaly','Nil','The liver is enlarged and measures about 185 mm in cranio-caudal span. It shows uniform parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. No focal mass lesion is seen. The biliary and vascular channels are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is enlarged and measures 175