sw',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It measures about 38.63mm in its widest AP diameter. It shows an intact endometrial plate echo.  No intracavitary collection is seen. Both adnexae and POD are within normal limits','Essentially Normal examination\r\nfollow up scan advised','2026-08-26 18:51:47','2026-08-26 18:51:47'),(392,20,'CYSTITIS',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder shows internal echoes. The biliary tree is also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion is demonstrated. The bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and show increased wall thickness of about 7.1mm. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features suggest cystitis.','2026-08-26 19:19:49','2026-08-26 19:19:49'),(393,14,'lumbar spond.','LUMBAR SPONDYLOSIS','There is straightening of the normal lumbar lordosis. Mild anterior listhesis of L5 over S1 noted. Anterior and lateral marginal anterior osteophytes are seen involving L1-L5 vertebrae more on L4. End plate sclerosis of L4 is noted. There is narrowing of the L5/S1 disc space.\r\nThe pedicles, posterior elements and the remaining disc spaces are within normal limits.\r\nThe vertebral alignment is normal.\r\nNormal para vertebral shadowing is seen.','Conclusion;  Moderate lumbar spondylosis. MRI suggested.','2026-08-27 12:50:32','2026-08-27 12:50:32'),(394,14,'knee OA','Knee pain','RIGHT KNEE.\r\n\r\n There is  spiking  of the intercondylar eminence of the tibia and articular margins of the patella. The remaining articular margins,bones density and alignment are within normal limits.\r\nNo features of dislocation is seen.','Conclusion: Mild osteoarthritis right knee.','2026-08-27 12:54:30','2026-08-27 12:54:30'),(395,14,'foot','domestic accident','LEFT  FOOT\r\n\r\nThere is a fracture involving the distal metatarsal bone of the first toe. the remaining demonstrated bones show normal density. Their outlines, articular margins and joint spaces are within normal limits. \r\nMild overlying soft tissue fullness/swelling is noted on the  foot.','Features distal metatarsal bone fracture of the first toe.','2026-08-27 13:11:45','2026-08-27 13:11:45'),(396,8,'Incomplete abortion','Pyelonephritis','The uterus is normal in size and shows mixed echo intra-cavitary collection of about 5mls in volume. No gestational sac is seen. \r\nThe Myometrial echoes are uniform. \r\nThe ovaries are normal in volume and shows random follicular distribution. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus or mass lesion is demonstrated.','Incomplete miscarriage.','2026-08-28 09:58:56','2026-08-28 09:58:56'),(397,8,'Grade II RPDx',NULL,'ABDOMINOPELVIC  USS.\r\nThe liver biliary tree, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, sizes and outlines. They measure about 95x42mm and 92x47mm in dimensions on the right and left sides respectively. They also both showed increased parenchymal echogenicity above the hepato-splenic parenchyma but the cortico-medullary differentiation is preserved. No calyceal dilatation or calculus is seen bilaterally. \r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. Severe ascites seen.\r\nNormal urinary bladder. The uterus and adnexae are normal\r\nBilateral pleural effusion is seen.','Features are suggestive of grade II renal parenchymal disease.','2026-08-28 10:07:28','2026-08-28 10:07:28'),(398,8,'PLCC',NULL,'The liver is enlarged and shows multiple poorly defined nodules of varying sizes demonstrated in both hepatic lobes, one of which measures about 97x63mm in size. No calcification or necrotic area is noted. The background liver parenchymal is normal. The intrahepatic veins and biliary ducts are within normal limits. Normal portal vein.\r\nThe gallbladder, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits. The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are normal in calibre and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal collection or mass lesion is seen. The appendiceal bed is within normal limits.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.\r\nThe prostate is normal in size and shows uniform parenchymal echopattern with intact capsule.','Features suggest PLCC.\r\nTriphasic abdominal CT is advised.','2026-08-28 10:23:44','2026-08-28 10:23:44'),(399,8,'Hydronephrosis','Right side pyelonephritis','ABDOMINO-PELVIC SCAN\r\nThe liver is normal in size and showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and echo pattern. No focal hepatic mass lesion is seen. The demonstrated hepatic veins and the IVC are not dilated. \r\nThe gallbladder, pancreas, spleen and the para aortic regions are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation. The right kidney shows moderate hydronephrosis with dilatation of the renal pelvis and proximal ureter. NO calculus is seen. The left kidney is normal.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No ascites or intra-abdominal mass lesion is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder and prostate are within normal limits.\r\nNormal prostate.','Right side moderate hydro-uretero-nephrosis ?due to distal ureteric calculus.  \r\nCT IVU is advised.','2026-08-28 10:30:04','2026-08-28 10:30:04'),(400,8,'GSD','Cyesis','The uterus is bulky and contains a single intact gestational sac in the fundal region with no fetal node or yolk sac seen within it currently. \r\nGSD=mm\r\nEGA=weeks + days\r\nEDD= 27/04/2027\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform. The internal cervical os is closed.\r\nBoth adnexae and POD are free. \r\nThe urinary bladder is within normal limit.','Single early intrauterine gestation at about weeks + days GA ?viability.\r\nRepeat scan after 4weeks for viability.','2026-08-28 10:57:51','2026-09-22 12:33:41'),(401,8,'Postdate','Postdatism','OBSTETRICS USS (BIOPHYSICAL PROFILE)\r\nSingle live intrauterine fetus. In longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular, FHR= 148b/m. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen.\r\nLiquor volume adequate and clear, AFI= 14cm.\r\nPlacenta is anterofundal, not previa and no retroplacental collection.\r\n               AVERAGE PARAMETERS\r\nBPD= 90mm, FL= 81mm, AC = 347mm, HC= 329mm \r\nGA = posdated 	EDD= posdated	  EFW = 3.89kg\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2 \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform. \r\nThe internal OS is closed.','Single live postdated intrauterine fetus  with satisfactory biophysical profile score.','2026-08-28 11:07:02','2026-08-28 11:07:02'),(402,8,'Hirsprung',NULL,'The demonstrated bowel loops gaseously distended and show fecal loading with feeble peristalsis. Normal wall thickening. No ascites is seen. \r\nThe liver is normal sized and showed normal parenchymal echopattern. No focal hepatic mass lesion demonstrated. The intrahepatic veins and biliary ducts are within normal limits. Normal portal vein.\r\nThe gallbladder, spleen and pancreas are within normal limits. The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated.','Features suggest Hirsprung disease with bowel obstruction.\r\nBarium enema is advised.','2026-08-28 11:56:25','2026-08-28 11:56:25'),(403,8,'Fibroadenoma',NULL,'Both breasts were examined using 7.5MHz transducer. \r\nThere is a well-defined iso-echoic ovoid mass lesion wider than tall noted at the subareolar  position of the left breast. It measures about 12x5mm in dimensions. No surrounding architectural distortion or calcification is demonstrated. The remaining left breast parenchyma and entire right  breast showed normal fibro-glandular echoes. \r\nThe axillae and the retromammary area are within normal limits. \r\nNo lymphadenopathy seen.','Left breast mass with benign features presumably fibroadenoma. \r\nImpression: BIRADS 2. (Benign findings)','2026-08-28 12:34:24','2026-08-28 12:34:24'),(404,8,'Breast NS','Breast lump','BOTH BREAST ULTRASOUND\r\n\r\nBoth breasts were examined using a 7.5MHz transducer. They showed normal fibroglandular parenchymal and stromal echoes. No focal breast mass lesion or collection seen.   The ductal system is also within normal limits.    \r\nThe retroareolar, retromammary areas and the axillary tails are also within normal limits. No lymphadenopathy seen.','Normal breast examination.','2026-08-28 13:10:19','2026-08-28 13:10:19'),(405,8,'CCF','CCF','CHEST\r\nThe heart is enlarged with multi-chamber configuration CTR= 66%\r\nThe aorta is unfolded.\r\nThe hilar vessels are engorged with features of upper lobe blood diversion. \r\nPatchy opacities are noted in both lung fields with thickening of the horizontal fissure ?due to interstitial edema. \r\nThe costo-phrenic angles are blunted.  \r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows.','Features are suggestive of congestive cardiac failure.','2026-08-28 13:14:37','2026-08-28 13:14:37'),(406,8,'CXR NS',NULL,'CHEST\r\nThe heart is normal in size and contour. CTR = 40%\r\nThe aorta and pulmonary vessels are within normal limits.\r\nNo focal lung parenchymal lesion seen.\r\nThe pleural recesses are clear.\r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows.','Essentially normal examination.','2026-08-28 13:20:13','2026-08-28 13:20:13'),(407,8,'PPCM','PPCM','CHEST\r\nThe heart is enlarged with multi-chamber configuration CTR= 66%\r\nThe aorta is not unfolded.\r\nThe hilar vessels are engorged with features of upper lobe blood diversion. \r\nNo focal lung parenchymal lesion is seen.\r\nThe costo-phrenic angles are free.  \r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows.','Cardiomegaly with multi-chamber configuration ?due to PPCM.','2026-08-28 14:36:47','2026-08-28 14:36:47'),(408,8,'Bronchopneumonia',NULL,'CHEST\r\nPara-cardiac and peri-hilar opacities are noted bilaterally.\r\nThe costo-phrenic sulci are free.\r\nThe heart is normal in size with CTR of 49%\r\nThe aorta and pulmonary vessels are within normal limits.\r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows.','Features are suggestive of bronchopneumonia.','2026-08-28 16:27:21','2026-08-28 16:27:21'),(409,9,'Incomplete abortion.','?incomplete abortion','The uterus is bulky measuring about 67mm in its widest AP diameter.  The endometrium is thickened, expanded and shows mixed-echogenic material within it suggestive of retained products of conception. The myometrial echoes are uniform. The internal cervical os is closed. \r\nBoth adnexae and POD are within normal limits. \r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus is noted\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion and ascites is demonstrated. The bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Features are suggestive of retained products of conception','2026-08-29 11:36:40','2026-08-29 11:36:40'),(410,9,'chest...BPN','NO CLINICAL HISTORY PROVIDED','There are peri-hilar and para-cardiac streaky opacities noted bilaterally\r\nThe heart is normal in size and contour. CTR = 51/113\r\nNo focal lung lesion is seen. \r\nBoth costo-phrenic sulci are free.\r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissues are within normal limits.','Features suggest bronchopneumonia','2026-08-29 12:23:43','2026-08-29 12:23:43'),(411,9,'ABD...PYELO','?cyesis','The kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They however show reduced parenchymal echogenicity with prominent pyramids more on the left side. The corticomedullary differentiation is preserved bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. It measures about 118mm in span. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline and are seen floating clear free intraperitoneal fluid collection. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated. The appendix is not demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It shows an intact endometrial plate echo.  No intracavitary collection is seen. Both adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Features suggest left sided renal inflammatory changes presumably due to pyelonephritis.','2026-08-29 13:07:31','2026-08-29 13:07:31'),(412,9,'ABD....BPH','Irritative and obstructive urinary symptoms','The prostate is enlarged and measured about 58. 38 mls in volume. It showed normal homogenous echopattern. It is also regular in outline with intact vesico-prostatic interface. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline with normal wall thickness and contained clear urine. \r\nThe kidneys normal in their positions, shapes, sizes and showed normal echogenicity. The cortico-medullary differentiation is preserved. No calyceal dilatation is noted. The right kidney bears two oval cortical cysts with internal septation noted in the middle and upper pole measuring about 14 x11mm and 13.7x9mm respectively.  No calculus is noted.  \r\nThe liver is normal sized and normal parenchymal echoes and texture with no focal lesion demonstrated. The intrahepatic biliary and vascular systems are normal. The gall bladder is normal in caliber and outline\r\nThe spleen and pancreas are within normal limits.\r\nThe bowel loops appear normal in caliber, peristalsis and outline.','Features suggest:\r\n1. Prostatomegaly presumably due to BPH\r\n2. Right renal complex cortical cysts(Incidental findings)','2026-08-29 13:19:05','2026-08-29 13:19:05'),(413,9,'testicular...left epididymo-orchitis.','left testicular mass r/o inguino-scrotal hernia','Both testicles were examined using high frequency transducer. \r\nThe left testicle is enlarged and showed reduced parenchymal echogenicity. They measured about 36 mm and 47 mm in their bipolar lengths on the right and left sides respectively. No focal mass lesion is noted.\r\nThe left epididymis is enlarged measuring about 33 x 25mm in size with associated probe pressure tenderness. The right is within normal limits. The hernial orifices are intact. No bowel loop is seen\r\nThe overlying skin is within normal limit.','Features suggest left epididymo-orchitis.','2026-08-29 13:50:51','2026-08-29 13:50:51'),(414,17,'Pelvic Incomplete Abortion 2',NULL,'The uterus is bulky measuring about 56.9mm in its widest AP diameter. Contain mix echogenic materials predominantly hyper echoic with clumps consistent of retent product of conception. \r\nThe internal os is closed. \r\nBoth adnexae and the POD are free','Conclusion:  Features suggest Incomplete Abortion.','2026-08-30 13:27:35','2026-08-30 13:27:35'),(415,17,'Abdomen Splenomegaly',NULL,'Normal hepatobiliary system, the pancreas and the Para aortic regions are within normal limits. The spleen is enlarged measure about 16.6cm but showed normal parenchymal echo pattern with no focal lesion seen within it.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe bowel loops are normal. No intraabdominal mass lesion or collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is intact.','Conclusion: Features are suggestive of Splenomegaly? Cause r/o TSS. \r\n                     Further clinical / laboratory evaluation are advised.','2026-08-30 13:37:13','2026-08-30 13:37:13'),(416,14,'Neck USS (normal examination)','Swelling on the neck','NECK SOFT TISSUE USS\r\n\r\nThe soft tissues of the  neck were examined using a high resolution transducer. They showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture.   No focal nodular mass lesion or collection seen. the thyroid glands are normal in size and echo pattern. the great vessels of the neck are within normal limits.\r\nThe underlying skeletal muscles of the neck and their fascial  planes are within  normal limits.','Essentially normal examination. Fallow up scan may be suggested if symptoms warrants.','2026-08-31 10:43:06','2026-08-31 10:43:06'),(417,14,'ocular cataract','RT TRAUMATIC CAT.','OCULAR ULTRASOUND.\r\n\r\nBoth globes were examined using a high resolution transducer. They showed normal size measuring about 22 x 20 mm and 23 X 22 mm in their diameters on the right and left sides respectively. \r\nThe anterior chamber is also within normal limits. The demonstrated lens are thickened bilaterally worst on the left side ware it appears ill-defined. The posterior segment of the left side showed multiple internal echoes within it.\r\nThe posterior segment on the right side showed clear vitreous contents. No internal echoes or evidence of retinal detachment seen. \r\nThe retrobulbar space, extra ocular muscles and the optic nerve are within normal limits.','Features suggestive of bilateral cataract with left side chronic vitreous hemorrhage.','2026-08-31 11:09:09','2026-08-31 11:09:09'),(418,14,'BREAST Abscess.','RT breast mastitis.','BREAST ULTRASOUND\r\n\r\n                                \r\nThe right breast was examined using high frequency probes.  There is an irregular area of hypo echogenicity which showed movement  in the upper quadrant of the right breast measuring about 32 x 17 mm in size suggestive of abscess. there is surrounding parenchymal inflammatory changes.   No focal solid mass lesion is seen on the  breast. There is associated thickening of the overlying right breast skin.  Few discrete right side axillary lymphadenopathy noted.\r\nThe pectoralis muscles and retromammary showed normal appearances.','Features suggest right breast abscess  with surrounding inflammatory changes. BIRAD 3.','2026-08-31 12:04:11','2026-08-31 12:04:11'),(419,14,'Abd. NSW','?UTI','ABDOMINO-PELVIC ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits. No intra-abdominal or collection seen. The liver is normal in size and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intra hepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echo pattern. The pancreas is also normal in size and echo pattern.  The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. The uterus is normal in size and showed uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. No cyesis or RPOC seen. The adnexae and POD re free.','Essentially normal sonographic findings. The possibility of PUD/GERD cannot be rule out.','2026-08-31 13:18:32','2026-08-31 13:18:32'),(420,14,'append. abscess.',NULL,'Abdominal Uss.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits. The spleen is normal in size and parenchyma echo pattern.The kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They showed normal parenchymal echogenicity  and cortico-medullary differentiation.\r\nThe appendix was not demonstrated however, a cloudy collection  which showed  mobility surrounded by inflamed omentum was demonstrated in the right ilaic fossa measuring about 66 x 55 mm in size suggestive of abscess.  Moderate probe pressure tenderness noted over the area.  the a adjacent bowel loops showed inflammatory changes. The remaining demonstrated bowel loops show  normal wall thickness and peristaltic activity.  The urinary bladder is  intact. the uterus is normal in size and echo pattern. the adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','Sonographic features highly favor appendiceal abscess.','2026-08-31 13:37:56','2026-08-31 13:37:56'),(421,14,'PELVIC GTD','PV Bleeding','PELVIC USS\r\nThe uterus is bulky measuring about 74 mm in its widest Ap diameter. The endometrium is expanded with heterogeneous collection measuring 85 ml in volume suggestive of retained product of conception. the myometrial endometrial interfaces are ill-defined.\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nBoth adnexae and The POD  is free.  \r\nThe urinary bladder is grossly within normal.','Features are suggestive of incomplete abortion. The possibility of GTD cannot be rule out. \r\nSerum PT and further evaluations suggested.','2026-08-31 13:55:41','2026-08-31 13:55:41'),(422,14,'ocular retinal detarch.','?RD','OCULAR ULTRASOUND.\r\n\r\nBoth globes were examined using a high-resolution transducer. They showed normal size measuring 22.9 x 21.5 mm and 22.1 x 21 mm in their diameters the right and left sides respectively. The anterior segments are within normal limits. \r\nThe  lens are also within normal limits. \r\nThe posterior segment of the right globe contained  echogenic strands parallel to and attaches to the posterior pole at the optic discs giving the so called “V” shape sign of retinal detachment. the left side vitreous is within normal limits.\r\nThe retrobulbar spaces, extraocular muscles and the optic nerves are within normal limits.','Sonographic features are suggestive of right side eye retinal detachment? cause.','2026-08-31 14:09:00','2026-08-31 14:09:00'),(423,14,'abd splenic infarct.','S/Malaria','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size. It measured about 10 cm in span. It showed normal echogenicity and texture. No focal intra hepatic lesion seen. The biliary tree is normal. The gall bladder is demonstrated and is normal sized and contained moderate sludge within it.\r\nThe spleen is  enlarged measuring about 12 cm in span. It however shows na wedged-shaped area of hypo echogenicity in the inferior pole measuring more than 34 x 21 mm in size suggestive of splenic infarct. no focal mass lesion is seen within it.\r\nThe pancreas was not visualized.  The para aortic and both peri-splenic and periportal regions are within normal limits. There is no peritoneal fluid collection.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their sizes, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.  \r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are normal in wall thickness, caliber and motility and mucosa. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline and wall thickness and contained clear urine.\r\nThe uterus is within normal limits.','1. Mild splenomegaly with suggestion of splenic infarct ? cause                       \r\n 2. Features of cholecystitis.  Further laboratory evaluation advised','2026-08-31 15:10:07','2026-08-31 15:10:07'),(424,14,'testicular epidymo-orchitis.','?','TESTICULAR USS\r\n\r\nBoth testicles are demonstrated. They measured about 26 x 15.8 mm and 32.3 x 18.6 mm in their sizes on the right and left sides respectively. No focal mass lesion is noted within them. However, The left testicle is enlarged and appear twisted  with a broad base in the region of the epididymis. the left side epididymis is also enlarged and showed mixed echo pattern. mild fluid seen around the left scrotal sac with surrounding inflammatory changes.\r\nThe left testes, epididymis and peri testicular fluid collection are within normal limits.','Features suggestive of left side epididymo-orchitis. The possibility of testicular torsion cannot be rule out. \r\nTesticular Doppler scan suggested.','2026-08-31 15:39:40','2026-08-31 15:39:40'),(425,14,'renal dysplasia','pain ? cause','ABDOMINO-PELVIC ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\n\r\nThe liver is normal in size and showed homogeneous echo pattern. The intra hepatic vessels and biliary channels are within normal limits. \r\nThe gallbladder, pancreas and spleen are within normal limits \r\nThe bowel loops are prominent and show fluid loaded most especially in the lower abdomen with thickened wall. They are however normal in outline and peristalsis. No free intraperitoneal fluid collection or mass lesion is seen.\r\nThe pancreas, spleen and para aortic areas are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in positions, and outline. They measures about 78 and 47 mm in bipolar length on the left and right side respectively. Both showed normal echo pattern with good cortico-medullary differentiation and central sinus echoes are preserved. The right kidney appear very small in size when compared with the left ? due to renal dysplasia.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It shows regular in outline and normal wall thickness.','1. Features of bowel inflammatory changes presumably enteritis. further evaluations suggested.\r\n2. Feature of right side small kidney ?  dysplasis? cause. further evaluations suggested.','2026-08-31 16:13:30','2026-08-31 16:13:30'),(426,14,'KUB N/S','Nephrolithiasis','K.U.B\r\nNo abnormal radio-opacity of calcific density to suggest a calculus demonstrated in the region of the kidneys, ureters or urinary bladder.  \r\nNormal bowel gas distribution pattern and caliber is seen.\r\nThe underlying bones, articular margins and joint spaces are within normal limits .','Normal examination. Abdominal USS is advised to evaluate the kidneys and urinary bladder and for features of back pressure effect.','2026-08-31 17:24:46','2026-08-31 17:24:46'),(427,13,'Twin gestation BPD','TWIN GESTATION','Twin viable fetuses seen. The leading twin is longitudinal lie, cephalic presentation and the 2nd twin is also is longitudinal lie but breech presentation.  One Placentae is seen on the anterior-fundal wall of the myometrium.  Amniotic fluid volume is clear and adequate in the sac of both twin. \r\nCardiac activity are good and regular.\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen. String sign is noted.\r\nAveragely  : FL =  55.2mm.     BPD = 76.9mm EGA= 30wks + 3days                            \r\nEDD=  06/11/2026\r\nAverage EGA = 30wks + 3days\r\nThe cervical os is closed\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline and wall thickness and contained clear urine.','Twin live gestation at about 30 weeks + 3 days GA(Diamniotic monochorionic)','2026-08-31 18:58:55','2026-08-31 18:58:55'),(428,13,'Abd Enterocolitis','Pyelonephritis R/O Enteritis','The liver is normal in size and outline. It showed normal parenchymal echotexture and echo reflectivity. The hepatic veins are within normal limits.\r\nThe gall bladder is filled with clear bile. It showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen. The biliary ducts are normal in caliber and luminal echoes.\r\nThe spleen is normal in position, outline and parenchymal echo pattern.\r\nThe pancreas is normal in size and parenchymal echo pattern. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe bowel loops in the lower abdomen are dilated with fluid loading, however it shows preserved peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion is seen. The region of the appendix is within normal limits. There is mild ascites noted.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They showed normal echopattern with good corticomedullary differentiation. No mass lesion or calculus is seen. The collecting system and ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly filled with clear urine and showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe uterus is normal in size and empty measuring about 35 mm in widest AP diameter. It shows uniform myometrial echoes and intact endometrial plate. The adnexae and POD are within normal limit.','Features are suggestive of inflammatory bowel changes presumably due to enterocolitis.','2026-08-31 19:23:17','2026-08-31 19:23:17'),(429,13,'Lesional USS LIPOMA','Right medial knee mass','LESIONAL SCAN \r\n\r\nUsing high resolution transducer, the medial aspect of the right knee. \r\nThere is a fairly oval well circumscribed hyper echoic lesion with multiple echogenic striation demonstrated within it. This lesion is noted adjacent to the knee. It measures about 58x26 mm in size. No cystic component or calcification noted.\r\nThe adjacent soft tissue and underlying bones are within normal limit.','Features are highly suggestive of medial right knee lipoma.','2026-08-31 20:50:56','2026-08-31 20:50:56'),(430,17,'Pelvic Complex Cyst',NULL,'The uterus is normal sized and empty measuring 47.8mm its widest AP diameter. \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform with an intact thin endometrial plate. \r\nThere is an ovals cystic mass with septation and mobile echoes within it measure about 45 X 114mm on the right, the left adnexium is free.  \r\nThe POD is empty.\r\nThe urinary bladder showed normal mucosal coating and clear urinary contents.\r\nThe liver, spleen, pancreas, para aortic areas and both kidneys are within normal limits','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of Complex Right Adnexal Cyst? Infected Cyst. \r\n                         Further Gynecological / Laboratory Findings are advised','2026-09-01 10:12:30','2026-09-01 10:12:30'),(431,17,'Pelvic Molar Gestation',NULL,'The uterus is bulky measuring 107.8mm in AP diameter. The myometral echoes are fairly uniform. The endometrial cavity is filled up with a multinodular variegated echo mass lesion with wholly and distorted areas of echo texture. Multiple cystic spaces are also seen within it with a suggestion of an amniotic inclusion membrane? chorionic. The endometrial/myometral interface is ill defined.\r\nBoth adnexae are within normal limits. The POD is empty.','Conclusion; Sonographic Features Suggests Molar Gestation. However Endometrial (Uterine Sarcoma) is a closed differential.  \r\n                    Serial HCG titer and further gynecological evaluation are advised','2026-09-01 10:14:36','2026-09-01 10:14:36'),(432,17,'Testicular Uss',NULL,'The right testicle is demonstrated using high frequency transducer while the left testicle is undecendent probably in the abdominal cavity.\r\nIs normal in size and outline with uniform medium-level granular parenchymal.\r\nNo focal intratesticular mass lesion or collection seen.\r\nThe peritesticular fluid is clear and within normal limits.  \r\nThe mediastinum testes, epididymes and the capsules show normal appearances.','Conclusion; Feature are suggestive of Left Undecendent Testis','2026-09-01 10:31:52','2026-09-01 10:31:52'),(433,17,'Leg NS','LEFT LEG','The demonstrated bones are well  mineralized and show regular outline.\r\nNo radiographic evidence  of  fracture noted.\r\nThe ankle joint is also within normal limits\r\nNormal overlying  soft  tissues.','Conclusion; Normal Examination. Rely on your clinical findings','2026-09-01 10:42:12','2026-09-01 10:42:12'),(434,17,'Umbilical Hernia',NULL,'Normal hepatobiliary system. The pancreas and the para aortic regions are within normal limits. The spleen is normal in size and parenchyma echo pattern. \r\nThe visualized stomach and the bowel loops are normal sonographically. However a hiatus communicating with the peritoneal cavity is noted at the supra umbilical region consistent with a hernia measure about 14mm \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nNo intraabdominal mass lesion or collection seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is grossly intact.\r\nThe uterus, both adnexae and POD are free.','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of Supra Umbilical Hernia. \r\n                      Further clinical evaluation are advised','2026-09-01 11:29:39','2026-09-01 11:29:39'),(435,17,'Pelvic Uss Hysterectomy',NULL,'The uterus is absent probably due to total hysterectomy.  \r\nBoth adnexae are absent.\r\nThe POD is empty. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine and no mobile echoes, the mucosal wall is intact\r\nThe liver, spleen, pancreas, para aortic areas and both kidneys are intact','Conclusion; Features are suggestive of Total Hysterectomy.\r\n                      Further Clinical Evaluation is advised.','2026-09-01 11:35:40','2026-09-01 11:35:40'),(436,17,'Abdominal Intraabdominal Sepsis',NULL,'There is grossly cloudy free fluid collection seen in the peritoneal cavity with areas of multi septated flagellations noted. \r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are seen floating within this cloudy ascetic fluid collection showing grossly thickened mucosa and hypo echoic walls. Very poor peristaltic activity is also noted. \r\nNo intrabdominal mass lesion seen. \r\nThe liver is mildly enlarged and showed changes of acute inflammation. No focal lesion is however seen within it. The spleen, pancreas and the para aortic region are grossly within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions and sizes. They both showed increase in parenchymal echogenicity worse on the right side with accentuated corticomedullary differentiation. \r\nThe urinary bladder is sonographically within normal limits.','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of Purulent Peritonitis with Multiple Organ Acute Inflammatory Changes? Secondary to Typhoid Perforation.\r\n                      Abdominal X-Rays (Erect and supine) are necessary for further evaluation.','2026-09-01 12:39:07','2026-09-01 12:39:07'),(437,8,'Bowel obstruction X-ray',NULL,'There is bowel dilatation in the center of the abdomen with prominent vulvulae conniventes and associated multiple air-fluid levels. Bowel gas is noted in the pelvis. The large bowel appears normal in caliber. No extra-luminal air.\r\nNo abnormal calcific density radio-opacity is seen in the regions of the kidneys, ureters and urinary bladder to suggest radio-opaque calculus.\r\nThe demonstrated thoracic, lumber vertebral bodies and bony pelvis appear within normal limits.\r\nNormal overlying soft tissue outline.','Features are suggestive of small bowel obstruction ?cause.','2026-09-02 11:57:24','2026-09-02 11:57:24'),(438,5,'cephal hematoma','?Cephal hematoma','LESIONAL SCAN (left parietal)\r\n\r\nUsing high resolution transducer, the left parietal area was examined.\r\nThere is hypoechoic collection expanding the left parietal scalp with internal mobile echoes. It seen beyond the transducer field of view, bounded by the sutural lines. It is not seen communicating with the intracranial cavity. The skull cortex is intact.','Features are in keeping with left parietal area cephal hematoma.','2026-09-02 19:19:00','2026-09-02 19:19:00'),(439,18,'Neck uss diffuse goitre','Thyroid disease','Both thyroid lobes were examined using high resolution transducer. They are both enlarged measuring 39 x 33 x 22mm and 37 x 21 x 11mm in their craniocaudal, mediolateral and AP dimensions on the right and left sides respectively equivalent to about 22mls. The showed heterogeneous parenchymal echotexture and reduction in parenchymal echogenicity. The isthmus is within normal limits.  No calcification or cysts seen within them. The thyroid capsule is preserved.  \r\nThe adjacent great vessels of the neck and  the overlying strap muscles are within normal limits. No lymphadenopathy demonstrated.','Diffuse bilateral thyroid enlargement with benign features.','2026-09-03 10:20:04','2026-09-03 10:20:04'),(440,18,'Oligohydramnious Obst uss',NULL,'Single live, intrauterine fetus.\r\nLongitudinal lie, breech presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is good. \r\nLiquor volume is severely reduced  with a single measurable pocket seen measuring about 1.8cm.\r\nInternal os is closed.\r\nPlacenta is posterior and within normal limits.\r\nBPD= 75mm, FL= 55 mm,   \r\nEGA= 29wks + 2days. \r\nEDD= 17/11/2026.','1. Single viable fetus at about 29weeks + 2days GA. \r\n2. Severe oligohydramnious','2026-09-03 10:36:56','2026-09-03 10:36:56'),(441,18,'Pyomyositis','Left thigh cellulitis/pyomyositis r/o fracture','The left thigh was examined on grey scale only using high resolution transducer.\r\ncomparative scans of the right thigh was also obtained.\r\nThere is subcutaneous tissue and skin thickening of the left thigh. The demonstrated muscles also appear enlarged with heterogeneous echopattern. Irregular turbid collection is also noted within the muscle layer. Real time compression revealed internal shifting.\r\nThe visualized femoral veins show normal calibre and outline with normal compressibility. No evidence of DVT on grey scale. The femoral artery is within normal limits.\r\nThe underlying femoral shaft cortex appears intact with no focal cortical errosion or distruption. \r\nThe contra-lateral thigh appears within normal limits.','Features suggest left thigh pyomyositis.','2026-09-03 13:11:13','2026-09-03 13:11:13'),(442,18,'PELVIC USS',NULL,'The uterus measures about 45mm in widest AP diameter. It shows homogenous myometrial echotexture. No intracavitary fluid collection is noted.\r\nThe endometrial plate is intact with normal endometrial/myometrial interface. \r\nBoth adnexae are within normal limits. \r\nThe POD is free.','Normal examination','2026-09-03 16:12:54','2026-09-03 16:12:54'),(443,13,'OBS CRL EARLY',NULL,'The uterus is Bulky containing single intact gestational sac with yolk sac and fetal pole seen within it, giving the diamond ring sign. \r\nCardiac activity is present. Liquor is adequate for GA\r\nCRL= 9.1 mm  EGA= 7 weeks \r\nEDD= 22/04/2027 \r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform \r\nThe Internal cervical os is closed. \r\nBoth adnexae are free. The POD is empty.\r\nNormal urinary bladder.','Conclusion: Single intrauterine gestation at about 7 weeks GA.','2026-09-03 19:34:58','2026-09-03 19:34:58'),(444,13,'OBS BPP','BPP','Single live intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation.\r\nCardiac activity is present and regular. \r\nNo gross fetal anomaly seen.\r\nAmniotic fluid is clear and adequate with a single deep pocket measuring about 56x52mm. \r\nPlacenta is posterior on the uterine body.  	\r\nBD = 90 mm, FL = 69 mm, AC = 354mm, HC = 326mm all corresponding to GA \r\nGA= 35weeks + 6 days   EDD= 02/10/2026\r\nEFW = 2815g	\r\nInternal os is closed.	\r\nBiophysical score:\r\nAFI = 2\r\nGross body movements = 2\r\nReflexes = 2\r\nRespiratory movements = 2','Single live intrauterine at about 35 weeks + 6 days GA with satisfactory biophysical profile of 8/8.','2026-09-03 19:43:32','2026-09-03 19:43:32'),(445,18,'intestinal obstrution',NULL,'The demonstrated bowel loops  are moderately dilated with thickened wall and show no peristalsis. To and fro movement is noted. Mild free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe liver is normal in size and echo pattern. The gall bladder contains clear content with regular wall thickness and outline. \r\nThe pancreas and para-aortic region are within normal limits.  The spleen is normal in size and shows uniform parenchymal echoes and outline.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They also showed normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly distended with clear urine and show normal wall thickness.','Features are suspicious of intestinal obstruction. Plain abdominal x-ray (erect and supine) is advised for further evaluation.','2026-09-04 10:30:29','2026-09-04 10:30:29'),(446,18,'Neck USS (normal examination)','?Foreign body.','NECK USS\r\nBoth thyroid lobes were examined using high resolution transducer. They are both normal in size  measuring 10 x 15mm and 9 x 12mm in their mediolateral and AP dimensions on the right and left sides respectively. They showed homogeneous  parenchymal echopattern. No focal mass lesion is seen. The isthmus is within normal limits.. The thyroid capsule is preserved.  \r\nThe adjacent great vessels of the neck and  the overlying strap muscles are within normal limits. No lymphadenopathy demonstrated.','Normal examination','2026-09-04 12:20:43','2026-09-04 12:20:43'),(447,18,'soft tissue neck',NULL,'SOFT TISSUE NECK\r\nThe normal cervical curvature is preserved. The demonstrated vertebral bodies, disc spaces, pedicles and the posterior elements are within normal limits. The demonstrated air column is normal in caliber and outline.  No para or pre vertebral soft tissue mass  or foreign body seen.','Normal study.','2026-09-04 12:25:09','2026-09-04 12:25:09'),(448,18,'Incomplete abortion.',NULL,'PELVIC USS\r\nThe uterus measures about 40mm in widest AP diameter. There is a mixed echo collection (about 20mls) in the endometrial cavity suggestive of retained product of conception (RPOC).\r\nThe myometrial echopattern is within normal limits.\r\nThe internal os is closed. \r\nThe adnexae are free. \r\nThe POD is free.','Features suggest retained product of conception/incomplete abortion.','2026-09-04 12:42:18','2026-09-04 12:42:18'),(449,18,'Fibroadenoma',NULL,'BREAST ULTRASOUND\r\nBoth breasts were examined using a 7.5MHz transducer.  Well defined predominantly hypoechoic  oval mass lesion is noted at the 11 ’o’ clock position of the left breast which is wider than it is tall. It measures about 30 x 22 mm in size. No surrounding architectural distortion or calcific focus is noted within. The remaining demonstrated quadrants of the left breast as well as the right breast showed normal fibroglandular parenchymal echoes. \r\nThe axilla and the retromammary areas are within normal limits.\r\nNo lymphadenopathy.','Features are highly suggestive of fibroadenoma of the left breast (BIRADS II).','2026-09-04 13:27:48','2026-09-04 13:27:48'),(450,15,'Pelvis uss (blighted ovum)','Bleeding PV in early pregnancy','Abdominal Uss.\r\nBulky uterus containing an irregularly shaped gestational sac with no embryonic pole within it. Poor decidual reaction is noted. \r\nGSD = 41.52mm. GA =  8weeks + 4days GA.\r\nBoth adnexae are free. Internal os is closed. \r\nThe POD is within normal limits.\r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine and shows normal wall thickness with regular outline. \r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes.','Features are suggestive of a blighted ovum.','2026-09-05 17:14:31','2026-09-05 17:14:31'),(451,10,'enterocolitis/uti/hydrocele',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size. It showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and normal echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are fluid loaded and showed to and fro movement of the luminal content. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with urine and showed thickened wall. No calculus is noted within it. \r\nBoth testicles are normal in size and showed medium level echopattern. No focal mass lesion or collection is noted within it. \r\nPeritesticular fluid collection is noted bilaterally.','CONCLUSION; \r\n1. Enterocolitis KIV bowel obstruction\r\n2. Cystitis as a component of UTI.\r\n3. Bilateral hydrocele','2026-09-06 13:22:59','2026-09-06 13:22:59'),(452,10,'complex adnexal cyst',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size. It shows uniform parenchymal echogenicity and normal parenchymal echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size 33mm, empty and shows uniform myometrial echopattern. It shows an intact endometrial plate.  No cyesis, intracavitary collection or mass lesion is seen.  There is a fairly oval multiseptated anechoic structure casting posterior acoustic enhancement demonstrated in the right adnexium. It measured about 32x29mm in size. The left adnexium and POD are free.','CONCLUSION; Right adnexal complex cyst.','2026-09-06 13:36:37','2026-09-06 13:36:37'),(453,10,'hepatic congestion/grade iii-iv renal parenchymal disease',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size measuring about 134mm in span. It showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and normal echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The intrahepatic veins and IVC are prominent. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. The right kidney is normal in echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation. The left kidney showed increased parenchymal echopattern with distorted corticomedullary differentiation. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. Mild ascites is noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is underfilled with urine with catheter balloon noted insitu. \r\nThe uterus is normal in size and echopattern. Both adnexae and POD are within normal limits.','CONCLUSION; Features suggest;\r\n1. Hepatic congestion with mild ascites presumably due to congestive cardiac failure. Chest X-ray is advised for further evaluation.\r\n2. Grade III-IV left renal parenchymal disease.','2026-09-06 13:44:14','2026-09-06 13:45:10'),(454,10,'nsw/pediatrics',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size. It showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and normal echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','CONCLUSION; Normal sonographic findings.','2026-09-06 13:46:29','2026-09-06 13:46:29'),(455,10,'n',NULL,'Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size. It showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and normal echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritioneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion or ascites is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in wall thickness and contained clear urine.','CONCLUSION; Normal sonographic findings.','2026-09-06 13:47:12','2026-09-06 13:47:12'),(456,10,'obs anomaly anencephaly/polyhydramnios',NULL,'OBSTETRICS ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\nSingle live intrauterine fetus in longitudinal lie and cephalic presentation. \r\nCardiac activity is present and regular. \r\nPlacenta is posterior-fundal. No subchorionic collection seen.\r\nLiquor volume is increased with AFI=466mm.\r\nFL = 66mm\r\nEGA= 33 weeks + 6 days, \r\nEDD = 19/10/2026\r\nThe internal os is closed.\r\nANOMALY FINDINGS;\r\nThere is non demonstration of the fetal calvarial bones and brain parenchyma with bulging of both orbits giving a Mickey mouse appearance on coronal plane (Frog eyes). Appearances are suggestive of anencephaly.','CONCLUSION: Single viable intrauterine gestation at about 33 weeks +6 days GA with anencephaly and polyhydramnios.','2026-09-06 14:25:54','2026-09-06 14:32:26'),(457,10,'bph',NULL,'ABDOMINOPELVIC USS\r\nThe prostate is enlarged. It measured about 54 mls in volume. It showed normal homogenous echopattern. It is also regular in outline with intact vesico-prostatic interface. \r\nThe urinary bladder is underfilled with urine.\r\nThe kidneys normal in their positions, shapes, sizes and showed normal echogenicity. The cortico-medullary differentiation is preserved. No calyceal dilatation is noted. No calculus is noted.  \r\nThe liver is normal sized and normal parenchymal echoes and texture with no focal lesion demonstrated. The vascular, and biliary channels are normal.\r\nThe gall bladder is distended with clear bile. The gall bladder wall is within normal limits \r\nThe spleen and pancreas are within normal limits.\r\nThe bowel loops appear normal in caliber, peristalsis and outline.','Features are those of prostatomegaly presumably due to BPH.','2026-09-06 14:30:29','2026-09-06 14:30:29'),(458,10,'pid/uti',NULL,'The uterus is empty measuring about 50 mm in its widest AP diameter.  The myometrial and endometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion or collection seen. The adnexae are within normal limits. The POD contains mild free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine and showed increased wall thickness.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Minimal free fluid in the POD ?PID.','2026-09-06 14:40:27','2026-09-06 14:41:15'),(459,10,'lumbosacral spine mild ls/calculus',NULL,'LUMBOSACRAL SPINE\r\n\r\nThere is straightening of the normal lumber lordosis is noted.\r\nThe demonstrated vertebral bodies showed anterior marginal osteophytes worst at L5 where irregularity and reduction in height is noted. The pedicles, posterior elements and inter-vertebral disc spaces are within normal limits.\r\nA fairly oval radioopacity of calcific density is noted in the left renal fossa suggestive of a calculus. \r\nNormal para vertebral soft tissue shadows.','Features suggest;\r\n1. Mild lumbar spondylosis.\r\n2. Left renal calculus.','2026-09-06 14:50:13','2026-09-06 14:50:29'),(460,10,'chest aortic knuckle/calcification/chilaidatis sign',NULL,'CHEST\r\nAllowing for patient\'s rotation on the radiograph;\r\nThe heart is normal in size and outline, CTR=62/135\'\r\nThere is prominence of aortic knuckle with a rim of aortic wall calcification noted.\r\nThe hilar vessels are intact.\r\nNo focal lung parenchymal lesion is seen.\r\nThe costophrenic angles are free.\r\nNormal bony thorax and overlying soft tissue shadows.\r\nThere is interposition of a bowel loop on the right side between the hepatic and hemidiaphragmatic shadow in keeping with Chilaiditi\'s sign.','Features suggest prominence of aortic knuckle with aortic wall calcification presumably senile','2026-09-06 14:58:51','2026-09-06 14:58:51'),(461,10,'chest xray ns',NULL,'CHEST\r\n\r\nThe heart is normal in size and contour CTR = 60/125. \r\nThe pulmonary vasculature is within normal limits\r\nNo focal lung parenchymal lesion seen. \r\nThe costophrenic angles are free.\r\nThe bony thorax and overlying soft tissues are within normal limits.','Normal examination.','2026-09-06 15:10:35','2026-09-06 15:10:35'),(462,10,'abdomen xry ns',NULL,'PLAIN ABDOMENINAL X-RAY \r\nNormal bowel gas distribution pattern and caliber noted.\r\nNo abnormal radioopacity is noted in the abdomen.\r\nNo features to suggest pneumoperitoneum.\r\nThe underlying bones are within normal limit.',NULL,'2026-09-06 15:14:30','2026-09-14 13:07:50'),(463,11,'MISSED abortion','cyesis','OBSTETRICS ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\nBulky uterus containing a single irregular gestational sac at lower uterine segment with a fetal pole  or cardiac pulsations are demonstrated.  \r\nGSD= 17.8mm,   EGA= 6 weeks + 0 days\r\nBoth adnexae and the POD are free. \r\nThe internal os is closed.','Conclusion:  Features suggest Missed Abortion at 6 weeks GA','2026-09-06 19:03:41','2026-09-06 19:03:41'),(464,11,'Pyelonephritis','ABDOMINOPELVIC USS.','The liver is normal sized and showed uniform parenchymal echogenicity and texture. No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection seen. The vascular and biliary systems are normal. The spleen pancreas and the Para aortic area are normal.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines, shape and sizes. The right kidney reduced parenchymal echogenicity and  with good corticomedullary distinction. No renal calculus is seen.\r\nNo intrabdominal mass lesion or collection seen.  The bowel loops are normal son graphically.\r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with urine, the mucosal wall is thickening, and no calculus is demonstrated\r\nthe prostate appear within norma limits.','Conclusion: Features of right  Inflammatory Changes most probably Pyelonephritis','20