 normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation. No calculus, mass or hydronephrosis is demonstrated. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It shows regular outline with normal wall thickness.  No calculus or mass is seen.','Normal examination\r\nKindly correlate clinically','2026-09-16 18:59:57','2026-09-16 18:59:57'),(564,14,'abd PCOS','amenorrhea','ABDOMINO-PELVIC ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\n\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. The uterus is normal in size and showed uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. No cyesis or RPOC seen. The adnexae are enlarged measuring about 34 and 40 ml on the right and left side respectively most likely due to PCOS.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits. No intra-abdominal or collection seen. The liver is normal in size and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intra hepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echo pattern. The pancreas is also normal in size and echo pattern.  The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally. The POD are free.','Features bilateral enlarged ovaries ? due to PCOS. TVS may be suggested for further evaluation.','2026-09-17 12:58:36','2026-09-17 12:58:36'),(565,14,'Missed abortion CRL','? Cyesis','Pelvic USS.\r\nBulky uterus containing a single, large gestational sac irregular in outline in the lower uterine segment.  A small fetal pole  and a large yolk sac but no discernible cardiac activity was demonstrated. \r\nThe myometrial echoes are within normal limits.\r\nCRL= 16.2 mm\r\nEGA= 8 Weeks + 2 days.\r\nInternal os is closed.\r\nBoth adnexae and the POD are free.','Conclusion:  Features suggest missed abortion,','2026-09-17 14:52:34','2026-09-17 14:52:34'),(566,15,'Pelvic uss (Missed abortion)','? Threatened abortion','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nThe uterus is bulky and contained a single gestational sac with a single fetus displaced in the lower segment. No fetal cardiac activity is noted. The gestational sac is irregular with poor decidual reaction.\r\nCRL=20.02mm,   EGA = 9wks + 1day\r\nThe internal cervical os is closed.\r\nBoth adnexae are within normal limits. \r\nThe POD is free \r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, pancreas, spleen and both kidneys.','Features are suggestive of missed abortion at about 9 weeks + 1day GA.','2026-09-18 13:46:01','2026-09-18 13:46:23'),(567,15,'Obstetric uss (Biophysical profile twin gestation)','Abdominal pain','OBSTETRICS USS   \r\nTwin live intrauterine fetuses both seen. The leading twin in longitudinal lie and breech presentation. The second twin is also in longitudinal lie and breech presentation.\r\nPlacenta is posterior-fundal.  Liquor volume is adequate. \r\nCardiac activity is good and regular (FHR= 143 and 148/min) in leading and 2nd twin resp.\r\nAv.BPD=  81.44mm,      Av.FL= 58.28mm        Av.AC = 282.54mm,      Av.HC= 294.42mm,       \r\nAv.EGA=  31wks + 6days,       Av.EDD=  14/11/2026\r\nAv.EFW=  1847.79g.\r\nSatisfactory gross body movement \r\nSCORES \r\nFine movement = 2\r\nAmniotic fluid = 2\r\nGross body movement = 2\r\nRespiratory movement=2\r\nTotal = 8/10\r\nThe internal os is closed.','Twin viable gestation at about 31wks + 6days GA with satisfactory well being','2026-09-18 15:01:15','2026-09-18 15:01:15'),(568,21,'Uterine myomas',NULL,'The liver is normal in size and showed regular outline with normal parenchymal echogenicity and texture.  No focal hepatic lesion is demonstrated. The hepatic veins are within normal limits.\r\nThe gall bladder is fled with clear bile. It showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. The biliary ducts are normal in caliber and echopattern. No focal lesion is demonstrated.  There is moderate epigastric tenderness.\r\nThe spleen and the pancreas are normal in sizes and echo pattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, ascites or adenopathy is seen. The region of the appendix is within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation. No calculus, mass or hydronephrosis is demonstrated. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It shows regular outline with normal wall thickness.  No calculus or mass is seen. \r\nThe uterus is bulky in size measuring 10 cm in AP diameter. There are multiple oval hypoechoec masses noted within the uterus and on the surface of the uterus. The largest measures about 90 mm x 75 mm in size and located in the posteriofundal region of the uterus. There are areas of cystic changes noted within some of the masses. No calcification is seen within it.  The endometrial plate is distorted.','Features suggest multiple uterine myomas','2026-09-18 19:36:45','2026-09-18 19:36:45'),(569,21,'NS ADULT',NULL,'The liver is normal in size and showed regular outline with normal parenchymal echogenicity and texture.  No focal hepatic lesion is demonstrated. The hepatic veins are within normal limits.\r\nThe gall bladder is fled with clear bile. It showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. The biliary ducts are normal in caliber and echopattern. No focal lesion is demonstrated.  There is moderate epigastric tenderness.\r\nThe spleen and the pancreas are normal in sizes and echo pattern.  The para aortic area is free.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, as