rgans are seen floating within the aforementioned ascites. \r\nThe urinary bladder is normal in outline and wall thickness and contained clear urine. \r\nThe uterus and adnexae are within normal limits.','Features suggest hepatic congestion with right mild pleural effusion + mild ascites presumably due to congestive cardiac failure.  Plain chest X-ray, ECG and echocardiography advised for further evaluation','2026-09-19 11:14:50','2026-09-19 11:16:26'),(572,21,'pelvic USS',NULL,'The uterus is normal in size measuring about 44 mm in AP diameter. It is empty and shows uniform myometrial echoes. The endometrial plate is intact. The myometrial-endometrial interface is preserved. The adnexae are within normal limits. No pelvic lesion is demonstrated The POD is empty.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately filled with clear urine. It shows regular outline with normal wall thickness.  No calculus or mass is seen.','Normal examination','2026-09-19 18:18:22','2026-09-19 18:18:22'),(573,6,'ABD RT Cyst','? Endometritis','Abdominal Uss.\r\nThe uterus is empty measuring about 49 mm in its widest AP diameter.  The myometrial and endometrial echoes are normal with no focal mass lesion or collection seen. A thick wall cystic lesion with internal septations is noted in the right adnexium suggestive of ovarian cyst. No solid component or calcification is noted. The left adnexium is within normal limits. The POD contains mild free fluid. \r\nThe urinary bladder contains clear urine with normal wall thickness and regular outline.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the spleen and pancreas. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in size, shape, and outline. They have good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes. \r\nThe visualized bowel loops show normal peristalsis and wall thickness. No mesenteric adenopathy noted. No intra-abdominal mass lesion seen.','Features suggest right ovarian cyst? haemorraghic.','2026-09-20 14:31:44','2026-09-20 14:31:44'),(574,6,'abd myoma','? Right 