line and echopattern. No focal lesion is seen within it.\r\nThe salivary glands are within normal limits.\r\nThe great vessels are normal in caliber and morphology.\r\nThe strap muscles and the sternocleidomastoids are within normal limits.\r\nNo cervical adenopathy is seen.','Mid-line simple cyst in the anterior neck most probably thyroglossal cyst.','2026-09-23 10:59:32','2026-09-23 10:59:32'),(601,12,'OCULAR N/S','OCULAR USS','Both globe were examined using a high frequency transducer.\r\nThe globes are normal in size with antero-posterior diameter of 22mm each \r\nThe anterior and posterior chambers as well as the lens are within normal limits bilaterally.\r\nThe lens is normal in position, thickness and echopattern.\r\nThe posterior segment showed clear vitreous bilaterally. No focal lesion is seen in the posterior segment bilaterally.\r\nThe retrobulbar areas, optic nerve shadows and extra-ocular muscles are within normal limits bilaterally.','Bilateral normal ocular examination','2026-09-23 12:32:18','2026-09-23 12:32:18'),(602,12,'ABDOMINOPELVIC AND OBST EARLY',NULL,'Normal hepatobiliary system is noted. The spleen, pancreas and both kidneys are within normal limits.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, ascites or adenopathy is seen. \r\nThe uterus is bulky containing single intact gestational sac with a single live fetus within it. Cardiac activity is good. Liquor volume is adequate and clear. Placenta is anterior\r\nCRL=52.78mm, EGA=12weeks+3days, EDD=04/04/2027\r\nNo gross fetal anomaly is seen\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform and internal os is closed','1. Normal examination.\r\n2. Single live intrauterine gestation at 12weeks+3days  GA in satisfactory wellbeing.','2026-09-23 13:07:02','2026-09-23 13:07:02'),(603,12,'foot x ray',NULL,'FOOT X-RAY\r\nThe bones showed reduction in density\r\nThere is spiking of the posterior of the calcaneum\r\nThe articular surfaces, articular margins and joints spaces are within normal limits\r\nThe alignment is preserved','Mild degenerative changes of the calcaneum.','2026-09-23 13:39:49','2026-09-23 13:39:49'),(604,9,'BREAST FIBROADENOMA','fibroadenoma','The right breast was examined using high frequency transducer. \r\nThe right breast shows an ovoid well-defined hypoechoic mass lesion with smooth margin, wider than tall with posterior acoustic shadowing measuring about 13x6mm in dimensions at 12 0’clock position suggestive of fibro-adenoma. No calcification or cystic portions noted within it.\r\nThe remaining right breast parenchyma show normal fibroglandular and stromal echotexture and echo reflectivity. \r\nThe retro mammary areas and axillary tail are also within normal limits bilaterally. \r\nThe ipsilateral axilla is within normal limits. No adenopathy seen.','Features suggest right breast mass with benign features presumably fibroadenoma.\r\n ( BIRAD-2)','2026-09-23 18:49:29','2026-09-23 18:49:29'),(605,14,'abdomen complex cyst.','? ovarian cyst','ABDOMINO-PELVIC ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits. No intra-abdominal or collection seen. The liver is normal in size and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intra hepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echo pattern. The pancreas is also normal in size and echo pattern.  The para-aortic area is free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation and normal central sinus echoes bilaterally.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. The uterus is normal in size and showed uniform myometrial echoes with intact endometrial plate. The right adnexium showed a thick walled cystic lesion