-28 13:01:07','2026-09-28 13:01:07'),(626,6,'abd M Spleno, cyst, enter','SCA','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe spleen is enlarged measuring about 155mm in span. it shows normal parenchymal echotexture. No focal mass lesion is seen. The liver is normal sized and showed   normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal.  \r\nThe pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops  in the lower abdomen using high frequency probe showed moderate fluid loading and slightly increased peristalsis. The wall thickness is increased.  No intra-abdominal mass lesion. Mild free peritoneal fluid collection seen.\r\n The urinary bladder is distended with urine that shows internal echoes with increased wall thickness.','Conclusion:  1. Features are suggestive of enteritis with cystitis.\r\n                      2. Splenomegaly? due to HbSS status of the patient? cause.','2026-09-28 13:32:00','2026-09-28 13:32:00'),(627,6,'obs crl, enetrit','? cyesis','OBSTETRIC USS\r\nBulky uterus containing a single intact gestational sac with a live fetal pole\r\nCardiac pulsation is noted. \r\nCRL= 9.7mm   \r\nEGA= 7weeks  \r\nEDD= 17/05/2027\r\nInternal os is closed.   \r\nBoth adnexae and POD appear within normal limits.\r\nThe bowel loops are fluid loaded with thickened wall and increased peristalsis. nil else of note.','1. Early viable intrauterine cyesis at about 7 weeks  GA in satisfactory well-being.\r\n2. Enteritis (maternal).','2026-09-28 15:35:39','2026-09-28 15:35:39'),(628,6,'abd F hep conges','ABDOMINAL SWELLING','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is mildly enlarged about 168mm in span.  It showed  normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic veins are dilated and seen draining int