nclusion:  Features are suggestive of Right Sided Inguinal Scrotal Hernia.','2026-09-29 09:41:10','2026-09-29 09:41:10'),(641,17,'Prostate BPH 2',NULL,'The prostate is demonstrated and its moderately enlarged measuring 3 X 4 X 3cm in its X, Y and Z axes. It showed fairly uniform parenchymal echo pattern and the capsule is intact. \r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine and showed normal mucosal wall, no calculus is seen.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in size, shape, position and outline. They showed normal parenchymal echogenicity and corticomedullary differentiation with no back pressure effect demonstrated.  \r\nNo intrabdominal mass lesion or collection seen. \r\nThe liver, biliary tree, pancreas and spleen are within normal limits.','Conclusion:   Feature are suggestive of Moderate Prostatic Enlargement presumably BPH.','2026-09-29 11:15:26','2026-09-29 11:15:26'),(642,12,'CERVICAL TB ADENITIS','LESIONAL PAROTID SWELLING','The neck was examined using a high frequency transducer.\r\nThere are multiple enlarged matted hypoechoic nodules in the left upper cervical region, left parotid and sub-mandibular region. Some of the upper cervical nodules showed areas of necrosis. No calcification is seen.\r\nThe right cervical nodal groups and the right salivary glands are within normal limits.\r\nThe thyroid gland is normal.\r\nThe great vessels and the strap muscles are grossly normal.','Left upper cervical, parotid and sub-mandibular adenopathy ?TB-adenitis','2026-09-30 11:08:39','2026-09-30 11:08:39'),(643,12,'NECK CERVICAL ADENOPATHY','LESIONAL PAROTID SWELLING','The neck was examined using a high frequency transducer.\r\nThere are multiple enlarged matted hypoechoic nodules in the left upper cervical region, left parotid and sub-mandibular region. Some of the upper cervical nodules showed areas of necrosis. No calcification is seen.\r\nThe right cervical nodal groups and the right salivary glands are within normal limits.\r\nThe thyroid gland is 