 mm in diameter ? due to cyesis. The adnexae and POD re free.','Features of endometrial thickening ? due to early cyesis. \r\nRepeat US suggested in 4 weeks time.','2026-10-01 19:37:32','2026-10-01 19:37:32'),(661,14,'Lipoma','LESIONAL USS','RIGHT LATERAL NECK SOFT TISSUE USS\r\n\r\nThe soft tissues of the right lateral neck = were examined using a high resolution transducer. There is an ovoid hypoechoic lesion beneath the sub cutaneous soft tissue overlying the muscle of right lateral neck.  The lesion showed echogenic striations. the remaining soft tissue are normal.  \r\nThe underlying skeletal muscles are within  normal limits.','Features suggest right lateral neck soft tissue lipoma.','2026-10-01 20:15:16','2026-10-01 20:15:16'),(662,14,'Breast mastitis','?Mastitis','BREAST ULTRASOUND\r\n\r\nBoth breasts were examined using high frequency probes.  Distorted fibroglandular parenchymal and stromal echoes were demonstrated in both breasts more on the right side. Also noted are prominent lactating ducts filled with content and converging to the nipple consistent with lactating breasts. The right  breast showed a wedge shaped area of thickened hypoechoic glandular tissues with equally thickened parenchyma stroma consistent with inflammatory changes around peri areola region. No focal mass lesion or lymphadenopathy is seen. There is associated thickening of the overlying skin.\r\nThe pectoralis muscles and retromammary showed normal appearances.','Features suggest bilateral breast mastitis in a lactating breast.','2026-10-02 12:37:14','2026-10-02 12:37:14'),(663,14,'shoulder anterior disl.',NULL,'LEFT   SHOULDER\r\n The  glenohumeral parallelism is  disrupted  with anterior and infero-lateral  displacement  of the humeral head consistent with an anterior  dislocation  of the  shoulder. the bones are normal in density.  mild overlying soft tissue swelling noted.','Left  shoulder anterior  dislocation.','2026-10-02 13:24:10','2026-10-02 13:24:10'),(664,14,'CHEST Aortic