 mm in size. The surround breast parenchyma showed  distorted fibroglandular echo pattern.  A large matted axillary enlarged lymph node are also noted in the right axillar. It measured about 33 x 30 mm in size.\r\nThe left breast and left axilla appear within normal limits. No intra-parenchymal/axillary enlarged lymph nodes are noted on the left side. mild skin edema  noted over the right breast.','Features are those right side breast multi-lobulted mass lesion with malignant features and ipsilateral axilla  matted lymphadenopathy.(BIRAD 4) Biopsy advised for further evaluation','2026-10-26 11:19:39','2026-10-26 11:19:39'),(800,14,'ABD URINE RETENTIOM FEMALE','?UTI','ABDOMINO-PELVIC ULTRASOUND SCAN REPORT\r\n\r\nThe urinary bladder is grossly distended with clear urine and and seen towering to the central abdomen, but showed normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. The uterus is bulky measuring about 81mm in AP diameter. it showed mild intra cavitary collection most likely due to luckia. it showed uniform myometrial echoes. The adnexae and POD re free.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and sizes. They both showed normal echogenicity, good cortico-medullary differentiation but showed mild hydronephrosis bilaterally due back pressure effect.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops appear grossly within normal limits. No intra-abdominal or collection seen. The liver is normal in size and showed normal parenchymal echoes and texture.  No focal hepatic mass lesion or collection demonstrated. The intra hepatic and extra hepatic vascular and biliary systems are within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen is normal in size and show normal echo pattern. The pancreas is also normal in size and echo pattern.  The para-aortic area is free.','Features are those of urine retention with back pressure on renal collecting system. Urgent catheterization suggested.','2026-10-26 11:29:43','2026-10-26 11:29:43'),(801,14,'ABD. CYSTITIS','?BPH/UTI','The liver is normal in size and outline. It showed normal parenchymal echotexture and echo reflectivity. The hepatic veins are within normal limits. No focal hepatic parenchymal lesion is seen.\r\nThe gall bladder is filled with clear bile. It showed regular outline with normal wall thickness. No focal lesion is seen. The biliary ducts are normal in caliber and luminal echoes.\r\nThe spleen is normal in position, outline and parenchymal echo pattern. The pancreas is also normal in size and parenchymal echo pattern. No focal lesion is seen.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and peristalsis. No intra-abdominal mass lesion, ascites or adenopathy is seen. The region of the appendix is within normal limits.\r\nThe kidneys are normal in position, outline and size. They showed normal echo pattern with good cortico-medullary differentiation. No mass lesion or calculus is seen. The collecting system and ureters are not dilated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is filled with urine showing internal echoes and thickened wall (5mm). No mass lesion or calculus is seen.\r\nThe prostate is normal in size and echo pattern. it measures about 23ml in volume. The capsule is intact.','Features suggestive of of cystitis. UTI.','2026-10-26 13:35:59','2026-10-26 13:35:59'),(802,14,'lumbar straightening.','LUMBAR SPONDYLOSIS','There is straightening of the normal lumbar lordosis. ? due to muscles spasm from pain. normal vertebral height and density demonstrated.\r\nThe pedicles, posterior elements and the remaining disc spaces are within normal limits.\r\nThe vertebral alignment is normal.\r\nNormal para vertebral shadowing is seen.','Reduction of normal lumbar lordosis presumably due to muscles spasm.','2026-10-26 16:58:33','2026-10-26 16:58:33'),(803,5,'NECK USS NORMAL','?Goitre','The thyroid gland is normal in size and shows uniform echotexture. \r\nNo focal lesion is demonstrated within it. \r\nThe demonstrated salivary glands appear within normal limits. \r\nThe strap muscles and blood vessels show normal appearances. \r\nNo focal mass lesion or collection demonstrated. \r\nNormal overlying skin.','Normal neck soft tissue examination.  Further evaluations suggested.','2026-10-26 20:30:13','2026-10-26 20:30:13'),(804,17,'Abdomen Cirrhosis',NULL,'The liver is small in size measuring about 12.4mm and shows distorted parenchymal echopattern. It also shows irregular margin. The intrahepatic biliary and vascular channels are not dilated. .   \r\nThere is moderate clear ascites with flouting bowel loops \r\nThe gall bladder, spleen and the pancreas are within normal limits. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outline and sizes.  They both showed normal parenchymal echogenicity with preserved corticomedulary distinction.  No renal calculus or back pressure effect seen. \r\nThe urinary bladder is within the normal limit\r\nThe uterus, both adnexae and POD are free','Conclusion: Features are suggestive of Chronic Liver Disease (Liver Cirrhosis) Presumably PLCC \r\n                         Further herpetological/clinical evaluation advised.','2026-10-27 09:58:17','2026-10-27 09:58:17'),(805,17,'Thyroid Scan',NULL,'Both thyroid lobes and the isthmus were examined using high resolution transducer. The left thyroid lobe and the left half of the isthmus are enlarged with multiple solid nodular and multicystic cystic mass lesions seen taking up the entire thyroid parenchyma. The size of this enlarged lobe measure about 18 X 26mm\r\nThe adjacent left carotid artery is displaced but not encased with the left jugular vein mildly compressed.\r\nThe right thyroid lobe is within normal limits measuring 14 x 13mm in its mediolateral and AP dimensions with no focal lesion seen within it.\r\nThe  overlying strap muscles are within normal limits.\r\nNo lymphadenopathy seen.','Conclusion;  Left Sided Multinodular/Multicystic Goitre with Benign Features. \r\n                    Thyroid function tests  are  advised for further evaluation.','2026-10-27 10:07:48','2026-10-27 10:07:48'),(806,17,'Breast Fibroadenoma',NULL,'The right breasts were examined using a 7.5MHz transducer. Showed normal uniform fibro glandular parenchymal and stromal echoes, with no area of architectural distortion, the right breast shows a thick-walled intramammary cystic in the 03 0’clock position. Its measures about 10 x 14mm in diameter. No calcifications seen.   \r\nThe retroarealar and, retromammary areas as well as the axillary tails of both breasts are within normal limits. \r\nNo lymphadenoapthy seen.','Conclusion; Features are suggestive of Right Breast Cyst? Fibroadenoma','2026-10-27 10:36:17','2026-10-27 10:36:17'),(807,17,'Obs at Term',NULL,'Single, live active intrauterine fetus  \r\nLongitudinal lie, Cephalic Presentation \r\nCardiac activity is regular. \r\nAmniotic fluid is clear and adequate for age. \r\nPlacental is posterofundal. \r\nBPD= 98.2mm, FL= 73.2mm    EGA = 40weeks + 1days\r\nEDD= 27/10/26','Conclusion: Single Viable Fetus at Term.','2026-10-27 10:52:58','2026-10-27 10:52:58'),(808,8,'TWINS','Cyesis','OBSTETRICS USS\r\nTwin viable intra-uterine fetuses are seen. Actively changing position.\r\nCardiac activities are good and regular. No gross fetal anomaly seen.\r\nThere are two separate placentae on the anterior and posterior upper uterine segments consistent with di-chorionic gestation.\r\nString sign is noted in keeping with di-amniotic gestation.  Amniotic fluid volume is clear and adequate.\r\nAVERAGE PARAMETERS.\r\nFL= 55mm, BPD=68mm.\r\nEGA =28weeks 2days      EDD= 18/01/2027\r\nThe myometrial echoes are uniform\r\nThe internal cervical os is closed.','Twin viable di-amniotic, di-chorionic intra-uterine gestation at about 28weeks + 2days GA.','2026-10-28 09:55:44','2026-10-28 09:55:44'),(809,18,'Cystitis men','?cystitis (UTI)','The liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted\r\nNo intra-abdominal mass lesion is demonstrated.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen.\r\nThe urinary bladder is mildly distended with urine containing internal echoes but show normal wall thickness. No calculus is demonstrated. \r\nThe prostate is within normal limits.','Features suggest cystitis (UTI).','2026-10-29 09:19:57','2026-10-29 09:19:57'),(810,18,'Mild knee osteoarthritis',NULL,'There is spiking of the lateral tibial intercondylar spine.  The remaining demonstrated bones show normal density and outline.\r\nThe  joint spaces and overlying soft tissue are within normal limits.','Features suggest mild knee osteoarthritis','2026-10-29 15:00:24','2026-10-29 15:00:24'),(811,14,'cervical spine','PPCM','CERVICAL SPINE\r\n\r\nThere is straightening of the normal cervical curvature. Early marginal osteophytic outgrowths are demonstrated on C5 - C7.  Spiking os Lushka joints also noted.\r\n The remaining vertebral bodies, remaining disc spaces, pedicles and the posterior elements are within normal limits. Normal para vertebral soft tissue shadows.','Features are those of mild to moderate cervical spondylosis.','2026-10-29 18:21:27','2026-10-29 18:21:27'),(812,14,'renal hydro','? pyelonephritis.','ABDOMINAL/ Renal USS.\r\n\r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, shape and outline and sizes. They measure 113 mm and116 mm in their bipolar lengths on the right and left sides respectively. They have normal  good corticomedullary differentiation bilaterally. However, the left kidney showed mild to moderate calyceal dilatation.  no calculus was demonstrated bilaterally. \r\nThe urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and is normal in outline and wall thickness.  the prostate is normal in size and echo pattern.\r\nNormal hepatobiliary system, the pancreas and spleen. no ascites demonstrated.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops are also within normal limits.','Features of left side mild to moderate hydrocalycosis? due ureteric calculus. CT IVU may be suggested.','2026-10-29 18:46:17','2026-10-29 18:46:17'),(813,6,'abd inguinal hernia','right inguinal hernia','ABDOMINAL USS\r\nThe liver is normal sized and showed   normal parenchymal echogenicity and echotexture. The intra-hepatic vascular and biliary systems are normal.  \r\nThe spleen, pancreas and the para-aortic regions are within normal limits.\r\nBoth kidneys are normal in positions, outline, shapes and sizes.  They show normal echogenicity and good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally. No calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe demonstrated bowel loops  in the lower abdomen using high frequency probe showed moderate fluid loading and slightly increased peristalsis. The wall thickness is increased.  No intra-abdominal mass lesion. No ascites is noted.\r\n The urinary bladder is distended with clear urine and showed normal wall outline.\r\nThe right inguinal canal is prominent with bowel loops noted within it. They howeveer, show normal caliber and peristalsis. The left inguinal canal in intact. No bowel noted in the scrotum.','Conclusion:  Features are suggestive of enterocolitis with unobstructed right inguinal hernia.','2026-10-30 09:00:36','2026-10-30 09:00:36'),(814,6,'breast mastitis rt','chronic right breast pain','Both breast were examined with high resolution transducer, there is thickened fibroglandular tissue in the right peri-areola region with reduced echogenicity. No focal mass lesion or collection is noted. The remaining fibro-glandular tissue are normal. The right axilla is normal. The left breast is within normal limits.','Features suggest right breast mastitis.','2026-10-30 09:27:31','2026-10-30 09:27:31'),(815,6,'abd molar','?','Abdomino-pelvic USS\r\nThe liver is normal in size and shows homogenous echotexture. No focal mass lesion is noted. The gall bladder and the biliary tree are also within normal limits. \r\nThe spleen and pancreas show normal size, parenchymal echogenicity and texture with no focal lesion is seen within. \r\nThe kidneys are normal in their positions, outlines and size. They also show normal echogenicity with good cortico-medullary differentiation bilaterally.  No renal calculus or back pressure effect is noted.\r\nThe bowel loops are normal in caliber and outline. No free intra-peritoneal fluid collection is seen. No intra-abdominal mass lesion is demonstrated.\r\nThe urinary bladder is moderately distended with clear urine. No calculus is demonstrated. It shows normal wall thickness.\r\nThe uterus is bulky measuring about 100mm in AP diameter. The endometrium contains mixed echoes collection about 73ml with varigated outline. No fetal parts or placental tissue is noted. POD and adnexae are free.','Features suggest molar gestation. Serum B HCG advised.','2026-10-30 10:13:52','2026-10-30 10:13:52');
